    {
      "id": "6b046fe32e04752522fe3aed",
      "name": "Vmcloudoor: a stealthy backdoor targeting the Chinese cloud",
      "description": "A sophisticated Linux implant called Vmcloudoor has been discovered targeting virtual machines hosted on Chinese cloud platforms, specifically Alibaba, Tencent, and Huawei. The backdoor disguises itself by mimicking legitimate cloud service processes and adapts its concealment profile based on the detected environment. It establishes command-and-control communications through Alibaba Cloud infrastructure and Gitee, using time-constrained beacons with machine fingerprinting. The implant features command execution, file transfer capabilities, and system inventory collection. It actively detects security products including EDRs and AVs, adjusting its behavior accordingly. Analysis of the infrastructure suggests development by a Chinese pentester, potentially for red team operations, with evidence pointing to structured development practices and OPSEC failures revealing internal domains and GitHub accounts.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-23T17:19:39.402000",
      "created": "2026-11-23T16:54:59.424000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
