    {
      "id": "6b0470884a0f9cab17aa31ff",
      "name": "MoldyRoost: A Malvertising Machine Built to Deliver iOS Exploits",
      "description": "MoldyRoost represents a large-scale malvertising operation delivering nation-state-grade iPhone exploit chains through programmatic advertising. Between May and November 2026, over 480 ad domains across six sub-clusters targeted 47 countries, with particular focus on Hong Kong, Japan, Singapore, the UK, and Turkey. The operation deploys four exploit kits (Coruna, DarkSword, SilkPath, and GhostWave) through cloaked landing pages that execute drive-by attacks requiring only loading the page on vulnerable iPhones. These kits target iOS versions 13.0 through 26, exploiting multiple zero-day vulnerabilities to exfiltrate cryptocurrency wallet seed phrases, keychain data, messages, and photos. The attackers combine sophisticated cloaking techniques with device fingerprinting to deliver exploits exclusively to iOS devices while showing benign content to others. A leaked repository revealed the operation's infrastructure, including version routers and channel-based attribution systems for stolen credentials.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-23T17:12:50.788000",
      "created": "2026-11-23T16:57:44.929000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
