    {
      "id": "6b046f701baf56a1277f3d3b",
      "name": "From Phishing Email to Azalea Agent: Uncovering a Multi-Stage Attack on Ukrainian Government Bodies",
      "description": "A sophisticated spear-phishing campaign targeted Ukrainian government bodies in October 2026, using a fraudulent email about financial assistance for military unit A1836. The attack employed a RAR archive containing a malicious LNK file that initiated a five-stage infection chain. The sequence began with a curl-based downloader, progressed through multiple encrypted stages including HIODropper and StageLoader, and culminated in the deployment of Azalea Agent 1.21.3, a .NET-based remote access trojan. The campaign utilized a C2 server at 151.244.30.176, historically associated with Iranian ISP Shatel before transitioning to a Canadian ASN. The infrastructure exposed multiple services including OpenSSH, NGINX, RDP, and potentially FRP-based tunneling capabilities. Despite thorough analysis, no definitive attribution to known threat groups was established, as Azalea Agent is a commercially available Malware-as-a-Service tool accessible to multiple operators.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-23T17:06:04.132000",
      "created": "2026-11-23T16:53:04.086000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
