    {
      "id": "6b03f0de3b5ed21d7846ec1e",
      "name": "Rotating Storefronts: Inside a Fake-Shop Network Gearing Up for Black Friday 2026",
      "description": "A sophisticated fake-shop operation has been identified preparing for Black Friday 2026, utilizing a Chinese-developed SaaS store builder platform called oemcart. The network operates 4,660 domains, with 3,415 observed between October and November 2026, rotating an average of 91 new domains daily. A single storefront was linked to 75 short-lived domains impersonating well-known retailers, primarily targeting Central and Eastern European, UK, and US shoppers. Aldi and Lidl are the most impersonated brands. The operation collects shopper contact details before payment attempts, while payment endpoints are supplied dynamically at checkout to evade detection. Infrastructure rotates between Cloudflare, Tencent Cloud, and Alibaba Cloud. A parallel network of 372 domains impersonates premium fashion brands using WordPress/WooCommerce. The operation employs multiple evasion techniques including daily domain rotation, server-side payment delivery, and CDN usage to hamper traditional detection methods.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-23T10:47:50.403000",
      "created": "2026-11-23T07:53:02.341000",
      "revision": 2,
