    {
      "id": "6b0055920249dca4654a73bb",
      "name": "October 2026 APT Attack Trends Report (Domestic)",
      "description": "During October 2026, multiple APT campaigns targeting South Korea were observed, primarily utilizing spear phishing and malicious HWP documents. Seven distinct attack types were identified, predominantly leveraging LNK files with PowerShell commands to deploy various payloads. Attackers employed cloud services like Dropbox, GitLab, and GitHub for command-and-control infrastructure and payload delivery. Common tactics included registry persistence, scheduled tasks, and DLL side-loading. The campaigns deployed remote access tools including XenoRAT, Xctdoor, and custom .NET-based RATs, alongside information stealers targeting browser credentials, cryptocurrency wallets, and system information. One campaign specifically targeted defense industry personnel using weaponized Hangul documents. Post-compromise activities focused on reconnaissance, data exfiltration, and establishing persistent remote control capabilities through various backdoors and legitimate remote management tools like MeshAgent.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-23T10:43:29.422000",
      "created": "2026-11-20T14:13:38.050000",
      "revision": 2,
