    {
      "id": "6b00d792e0f0c62062da298f",
      "name": "Dialing for Data: Inside the Com's High-Profile Heists",
      "description": "Multiple threat actors affiliated with Com have conducted persistent vishing campaigns targeting data-rich organizations since August 2026, leading to data theft and extortion attempts. The operations primarily focused on financial services, healthcare, and legal sectors in the United States, United Kingdom, and Australia. Attackers employed social engineering techniques, posing as IT support to direct victims to adversary-in-the-middle proxies that captured credentials and MFA tokens. Following initial access, threat actors established persistence through unauthorized MFA device enrollment, exfiltrated data using scripted methods and native cloud utilities, and sent extortion demands via internal communication channels. Two newly identified activity clusters, CL-CRI-1264 and CL-CRI-1274, demonstrated advanced techniques including malicious browser extensions with keylogging and remote control capabilities. These cybercriminals have shifted away from encryption-based extortion, enabling faster operations w...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-23T07:57:12.406000",
      "created": "2026-11-20T23:28:18.298000",
