    {
      "id": "6b0114de9281959005e481a4",
      "name": "Inside a Gentlemen Ransomware-Linked Intrusion",
      "description": "A deception alert revealed a multi-week intrusion initiated through compromised credentials on an internet-facing Citrix VDI environment lacking MFA enforcement. The threat actor, whose credentials appeared in stealer-logs five days prior, systematically mapped Active Directory, executed large-scale account enumeration exceeding 41,000 queries, and accessed files containing plaintext passwords and tokens. The intrusion escalated to domain-level compromise when the operator reset and re-enabled a disabled Domain Admin account, modified privileged passwords, and added a service identity to Domain Admins group. Tools including SoftPerfect Network Scanner and FileZilla were staged and masqueraded. Approximately 270 SFTP connections to external servers were observed, indicating potential data exfiltration. The case demonstrates how stealer-log exposures combined with absent MFA and insecure credential storage enable rapid privilege escalation to domain administrator control.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-23T07:51:29.978000",
      "created": "2026-11-21T03:49:50.904000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
