    {
      "id": "6ada5f1e1071ed1bf4072f30",
      "name": "StealC Is Back, and This Time It's a RAT",
      "description": "Four months after Operation Endgame dismantled StealC in June, its seller returned in October with Stadia, a full-featured remote access trojan that incorporates StealC's code verbatim. Unlike its predecessor, Stadia offers comprehensive remote administration capabilities including hidden desktop control, live command shell, file explorer, process manager, and in-memory loader, with the original StealC stealer functioning as one of six modules. The operator targets former StealC customers by offering a free month on the top-tier subscription priced at $900 monthly. Analysis reveals the binary shares byte-for-byte code with StealC version 3.5, particularly the Chromium App-Bound Encryption helper. The agent communicates via plain HTTP to three hardcoded IP addresses, uses RC4 encryption with Base64 encoding, and establishes persistence through hidden scheduled tasks under C:\\ProgramData\\ with randomized directory names impersonating legitimate updaters. The transformation from simple infostealer to full RAT...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-21T19:00:26.421000",
      "created": "2026-10-22T19:08:14.184000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
