    {
      "id": "6ada5f1e04fbf3494e4114a7",
      "name": "MythicRatatoskr: An Yggdrasil-enabled backdoor deployed in a UAC-0099-Sandworm collaboration",
      "description": "On July 16th, 2025, UAC-0099 conducted a spearphishing attack against a Ukrainian grain logistics company, deploying the MATCHWOK backdoor. The following day, attackers introduced MythicRatatoskr, a previously undocumented Go-based backdoor utilizing the Yggdrasil mesh network for command and control communications. This decentralized network enables end-to-end encrypted IPv6 traffic between nodes, complicating detection efforts. Approximately two months later, on September 17th, 2025, Sandworm executed a destructive data-wiping attack using the SDelete utility deployed via Active Directory Group Policy. This incident represents documented cooperation between UAC-0099, acting as an initial access broker, and Sandworm, responsible for the destructive phase. The MythicRatatoskr backdoor supports standard backdoor functionality including command execution, file transfer, screenshot capture, and SOCKS5 proxying capabilities, marking the first documented case of state-aligned actors exploiting Yggdrasil infrast...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-21T19:00:26.421000",
      "created": "2026-10-22T19:08:14.735000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "UAC-0099, Sandworm",
