    {
      "id": "6ada1e58491e58bb903b7604",
      "name": "Hunting Leaked PHP2Shell RCE Across Open Directories (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619)",
      "description": "Two critical PHP remote code execution vulnerabilities, CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619, both rated CVSS v4.0 9.2, leaked before their scheduled patch on October 21, 2026. The flaws involve out-of-memory corruption in PHP core through multipart/form-data parsing, exploitable via session.upload_progress without authentication. Scanning began approximately 20 minutes after the patch release, with activity traced to a Mirai-style IoT botnet. Analysis of attacker infrastructure revealed approximately ten workspaces staging php2shell tooling, targeting WooCommerce, WHMCS, and Magento platforms. Despite widespread exposure affecting over 683,000 IPs running vulnerable PHP versions, no successful in-the-wild exploitation was confirmed as of October 21, 2026. The technical difficulty of achieving reliable code execution on systems with address-space randomization limited successful compromises.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-21T14:02:03.875000",
      "created": "2026-10-22T14:31:52.128000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
