    {
      "id": "6ad964720fdac83866db4a7d",
      "name": "Inside a Global AI-Assisted Hacking Campaign",
      "description": "In October 2026, a Chinese-speaking threat actor conducted widespread AI-assisted cyberattacks combining the ARTEX penetration testing framework with multiple AI coding assistants including Claude Code, Codex, and Grok. The attacks, initially reported as targeting South Korean financial institutions, affected organizations globally across multiple industries including finance, retail, education, cryptocurrency, and telecommunications. Custom synchronization scripts maintained investigation context across AI sessions, while specialized agents divided reconnaissance and exploitation tasks. Prompts revealed requests for bulk personal data, transaction records, and mobile phone numbers, alongside questions about selling stolen information on underground markets. The workflow incorporated peer review between AI models, with GLM instructed to audit DeepSeek findings. Targeting spanned over 20 countries across Asia, Africa, Europe, and North America, indicating financially-motivated opportunistic attacks.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-21T01:03:03.910000",
      "created": "2026-10-22T01:18:42.723000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [],
      "tags": [
