    {
      "id": "6ad8d8853d4b5de3946bd006",
      "name": "Stray Cat, Open Doors: How k0t Wanders Through the Network Edge",
      "description": "Group-IB and NyxLab uncovered a large-scale campaign by threat actor k0t exploiting FortiGate, FortiWeb, and Palo Alto GlobalProtect edge devices to harvest credentials and establish persistent access. The operation involves exploiting CVE-2025-64446 in FortiWeb and CVE-2026-0257 in GlobalProtect, alongside brute-forcing attacks using custom tools. Over 70,000 exposed credentials were discovered, with victims spanning multiple industries globally. Post-compromise activities include credential theft, Active Directory enumeration, and data exfiltration via Rclone to cloud storage. Persistence is maintained through MeshCentral, AdaptixC2, and various RMM tools including Atera and AnyDesk. The campaign shows overlaps with Qilin and The Gentlemen ransomware groups, suggesting k0t may operate as an Initial Access Broker, though direct affiliation remains unconfirmed.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T15:01:55.620000",
      "created": "2026-10-21T15:21:41.901000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "k0t",
