    {
      "id": "6b0041b6f254e5321e03a189",
      "name": "UAT-12643: Suspected North Korea-aligned actor blends blockchain resilience with targeted infostealing",
      "description": "A financially motivated threat group designated UAT-12643 has been discovered operating malicious infrastructure targeting cryptocurrency holders, gaming platform users, and VoIP software operators. The actor deploys multiple payloads including the Overlord RAT, Python-based Good Game infostealer, and a multi-cryptocurrency clipboard hijacker. The Overlord RAT employs an innovative command-and-control resilience technique by embedding encrypted server URLs in Solana blockchain transaction memos. Potential victims are located primarily in Europe based on file harvesting capabilities targeting English, French, Spanish, and Portuguese documents. The campaign demonstrates overlaps with known North Korean APT tactics, particularly through the use of Overlord RAT and Solana blockchain techniques previously attributed to Lazarus Group and UNK_DeadDrop cluster. Lure themes suggest targeting of finance staff, VoIP operators, and cryptocurrency users across multiple sectors.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:49:25.229000",
      "created": "2026-11-20T12:48:53.126000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "UAT-12643",
