    {
      "id": "6b00038798ea9ab49aa7e331",
      "name": "N0N Ransomware Group: Victims, Leak Site, TTPs & IOCs",
      "description": "N0N is a financially motivated cyber extortion group that emerged in September 2026, employing data theft and extortion tactics without using traditional encryption methods. The group leverages compromised credentials obtained from third-party infostealer campaigns to infiltrate corporate networks. Once inside, they exfiltrate sensitive information including Active Directory mappings and legal documents, then threaten public disclosure via dark web leak sites to coerce ransom payments. N0N targets multiple sectors including investment services, telecommunications, retail, education, and pharmaceuticals across 54 countries. Their approach avoids conventional file encryption, instead manipulating victim data through administrative tools, making detection more challenging for traditional security controls.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:43:43.089000",
      "created": "2026-11-20T08:23:35.132000",
