    {
      "id": "6b001df518d887db38d8b386",
      "name": "Inside the 'Party' Panel: How Fraudsters Rent Android Banking Trojans to Target Indian Bank Customers",
      "description": "A multi-tenant malware-as-a-service platform enables fraudsters to deploy fake Google Play pages and branded Android banking trojans targeting Indian financial institutions. The operation, discovered via an unprotected server, hosted 50 tenant accounts with 34 active paid licenses targeting customers of six Indian banks and card issuers. Victims are lured through convincing fake Play Store pages that harvest card details, CVV, and personal information before delivering a two-stage malware. The dropper bypasses Android 13+ security by impersonating the Play Store installation process, while the hidden payload steals SMS-based OTPs, uploads sensitive photos, and redirects phone calls using call-forwarding codes. The infrastructure leverages Firebase and Telegram for command-and-control, with all indicators pointing to an India-based operator exploiting Indian hosting providers and targeting domestic financial customers and government service users.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:35:42.217000",
      "created": "2026-11-20T10:16:21.010000",
