    {
      "id": "6afd6e9a1376c3625c410a29",
      "name": "Unsolicited audits: how AuditTeam masks ransomware",
      "description": "AuditTeam is an active threat group operating since January 2026, using the sophisticated OpsAgent framework to compromise organizations across multiple countries including Russia, Italy, Philippines, Hong Kong, Senegal, Finland, and China. The group demands an 'Audit & Consulting fee' for vulnerability reports, masking ransomware operations as security consulting. OpsAgent evolved from C++ to Rust implementation, providing extensive capabilities including file system management, process injection, privilege escalation, keylogging, screenshot capture, and network pivoting. The framework uses AWS CloudFront subdomains for command-and-control, discovered via GitHub repositories. Two specialized modules extend functionality: an AV/EDR killer using a signed Beijing Jiangmin Antivirus driver to terminate security products, and a cryptor module encrypting files with AES-CBC or ChaCha20 while targeting database processes. The transition to Rust and evidence of LLM-assisted development suggests evolving toolchain ...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:29:06.769000",
      "created": "2026-11-18T09:23:38.448000",
