    {
      "id": "6afe6009a92c5d101710a3da",
      "name": "Attackers Exploit Optimizely Flaw To Inject Malicious JavaScript",
      "description": "On November 16, 2026, an attacker exploited a vulnerability in Optimizely's Web Experimentation account signup flow, allowing unauthorized modification of the Project JavaScript field. This enabled injection of malicious JavaScript into customer projects, which was then delivered to website visitors through legitimate Optimizely snippets served from their CDN. The malicious payload was designed to replace cryptocurrency wallet addresses for Bitcoin, Ethereum, Tron, Solana, Litecoin, Toncoin, Bitcoin Cash, and Dogecoin. It also performed payment card skimming, cookie theft, screen capture functionality, and delivered iOS exploit kits (Coruna and DarkSword) targeting iPhones and iPads. ThreatLabz identified over 450 unique domains and 3,000 URLs serving the malicious script, affecting multiple industries including airlines, automotive, banking, e-commerce, insurance, media, real estate, retail, telecommunications, and technology sectors. Optimizely blocked the vulnerable path, removed injected code, and rese...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:23:33.964000",
      "created": "2026-11-19T02:33:45.160000",
