    {
      "id": "6afedbdf974daf92590f1394",
      "name": "One Phishing Kit, 29 Fake Banks",
      "description": "Since late September 2026, a phishing campaign has been deploying fake online banking websites using a single template kit. The operation created 29 unique fake-bank domains with professional-looking pages designed to harvest credentials and personally identifiable information. Each site features identical artifacts including the same tagline, bank routing number, and support phone number, with only bank names swapped. Domains use cheap TLDs and are registered on disposable infrastructure. Victims were primarily located in North America, followed by Europe and Asia, with finance and banking organizations representing nearly half of affected targets. One-third of domains had zero antivirus detection at discovery time. The campaign uses a purchased PHP banking-scam kit, originally branded as EMENDY INVEST. Operators build fake business ecosystems around these domains to appear in search results and enhance legitimacy.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:11:39.714000",
      "created": "2026-11-19T11:22:07.090000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
