    {
      "id": "6afeddb30eb6cad456c0630b",
      "name": "Major African Stock Exchange Targeted in AI-Assisted Attack",
      "description": "Attackers deployed a sophisticated 41-module PowerShell toolkit against an African stock exchange, exhibiting strong indicators of AI-assisted development. The toolkit operated for just over three minutes in September 2026, systematically hunting credentials and testing them against the exchange's investment API and securities depository gateway. Each module utilized identical scaffolding and hex-encoded DNS exfiltration to unique subdomains of a public out-of-band testing service. Six persistence implants attributed to China-linked group Witchetty were discovered on the same server, with earliest activity dating to April 2026. The toolkit targeted cloud credentials, database connections, SharePoint, SCCM, and TFS servers, focusing on systems close to financial operations. While Witchetty is traditionally an espionage group, the financial targeting suggests possible cybercrime motivation, though espionage cannot be ruled out.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:09:10.461000",
      "created": "2026-11-19T11:29:55.933000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Witchetty",
