    {
      "id": "6aff044fb4b53217d494e9a1",
      "name": "Inside Turla's Cereal: 12 Exchange loaders, older traces and new ways to hunt",
      "description": "In November 2026, researchers disclosed Cereal, a modular espionage toolset deployed by the Russia-aligned Turla group against Microsoft Exchange servers at government organizations in Kazakhstan and Romania. The operation targeted email communications involving NATO and European Union institutions through stealthy components that avoided traditional detection methods. CerealNeuron listened for specially crafted web requests on compromised servers, while CerealBox intercepted selected emails within Exchange's transport pipeline without registering new agents. Analysis identified 12 related loader files, with evidence dating back to 2022. The toolset employed DLL side-loading, impersonated legitimate Windows files, and operated within trusted infrastructure to avoid outbound beacons. Multiple naming conventions across security vendors complicated detection efforts, requiring defenders to correlate file metadata, structural hashes, and behavioral analysis rather than relying on single indicators.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T12:07:50.997000",
      "created": "2026-11-19T14:14:39.199000",
