    {
      "id": "6aff569e13ea32795e9750a1",
      "name": "ARMORY CASTLE Exploits vSphere",
      "description": "In September 2026, the suspected PRC-nexus threat actor ARMORY CASTLE exploited CVE-2026-123890, a zero-day vulnerability in VMware vCenter Server, following their initial exploitation of CVE-2026-102764 in BeyondTrust Remote Support. The group demonstrated sophisticated post-exploitation capabilities by deploying five newly identified malware families: BONESAW (a Golang exploitation utility), SAWSNAKE (a SAML authentication bypass tool), SLIMSAVAGE and CAGEMATCH (webshells), and BEARBONES (a backdoored SSH server). ARMORY CASTLE leveraged these tools to conduct reconnaissance targeting VMware infrastructure, escalate privileges, establish persistence, steal credentials including vCenter master keys and PostgreSQL passwords, and ultimately extract sensitive data from ESXi guest VMs. The campaign showcases the threat actor's deep platform expertise across multiple appliance types and substantial resource backing, utilizing two zero-days and three specialized malware sets in a single operation.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T11:57:10.511000",
      "created": "2026-11-19T20:05:50.076000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "UTA0178",
