    {
      "id": "6ad8968ddeccc0f490a19622",
      "name": "Autonomous LLMjacking: 'Skynet' Agent Hijacks Exposed AI Models to Run Attacks",
      "description": "Attackers have developed an autonomous offensive agent that scans the internet for exposed large language model endpoints and hijacks them to execute attacks. The agent is equipped with 74 offensive tools covering reconnaissance, exploitation of web frameworks including VS Code, Django, Jupyter, Laravel, Supabase, Next.js, Flask/Werkzeug, database theft through Prisma, credential harvesting, and cryptocurrency mining. Once connected to an unprotected model, it operates unattended for up to 100,000 steps without human approval. The operators use jailbreak techniques to bypass safety controls, redefining credential theft as routine development work. Victims include model owners who pay for computing power and compromised servers stripped of data and used for Monero mining. The activity was captured through an AI honeypot that recorded the complete instruction set, revealing a self-directed cybercrime operation targeting internet-facing AI services without authentication.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-20T10:00:15.943000",
      "created": "2026-10-21T10:40:13.342000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
