    {
      "id": "6ad791051c8d94c4c32e8ad7",
      "name": "Ukraine's State Data-Exchange System Targeted by Russian-Speaking Operator via Graylog Log4Shell",
      "description": "Between May and September 2026, a Russian-speaking operator systematically targeted Ukraine's state data-exchange infrastructure by exploiting Log4Shell vulnerabilities in Graylog servers. The attacker swept 9.1 million Ukrainian IP addresses, filtering 7,576 live hosts to identify systems running UXP Verifier, a component of the national data-exchange platform. Using a two-stage CommonsBeanutils2 deserialization chain delivered through Graylog's sessions API, the operator gained access to at least two organizations, including a logging server containing 6.8 million documents from Ukraine's state data-exchange system. The operation was exposed when the attacker accidentally served their working directory over HTTP for 17 hours, revealing reconnaissance tools, shell history, exploit code, and access logs. While the operator queried transaction indices and demonstrated prior knowledge of the system's schema, no data exfiltration was directly observed. The campaign also included failed exploitation attempts a...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-19T16:01:05.266000",
      "created": "2026-10-20T16:04:21.249000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
