      "id": "6ad79104128abd6fe9532c09",
      "name": "Threat Brief: Active Exploitation of PAN-OS CVE-2026-0257",
      "description": "Active exploitation of PAN-OS vulnerability CVE-2026-0257 has been observed, targeting GlobalProtect portal and gateway components. The authentication bypass flaw allows unauthorized attackers to circumvent security controls and establish VPN connections. Ransomware operators including Spikey Scorpius (Qilin) and Tarnished Scorpius (Inc), along with Settra ransomware actors, are exploiting this vulnerability to gain initial network access. Following successful exploitation, threat actors bypass multi-factor authentication, conduct internal reconnaissance using remote monitoring tools, move laterally via RDP and SMB, and stage additional tooling for credential harvesting and ransomware deployment. A sophisticated tactic observed involves pivoting directly to the virtualization layer, accessing vCenter management appliances, disabling security controls on ESXi hypervisors, and performing offline credential dumping against domain controller virtual disks. Multiple industries have been impacted including educa...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-19T16:01:05.266000",
      "created": "2026-10-20T16:04:20.723000",
