    {
      "id": "6ad77e2e717e0153aa2fda49",
      "name": "Active Exploitation of CVE-2026-110936 in Siemens Software Center",
      "description": "A DLL side-loading vulnerability in Software Center version 3.5.8.7 is being actively exploited by attackers. The threat actors distribute a genuine, digitally signed copy of the application alongside malicious DLL files through unofficial channels. When executed, the vulnerable version loads the attacker-supplied DLLs without validation, enabling malicious code execution. The attack vector involves ClickFix social engineering tactics, tricking users into executing commands. The campaign uses specific infrastructure for payload hosting and command-and-control operations. Version 4.0.9.8 patches this vulnerability, with automatic updates applied upon application restart. No official systems or distribution channels were compromised during this campaign.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-19T14:01:03.768000",
      "created": "2026-10-20T14:43:58.172000",
