    {
      "id": "6afe21487f55b1567b331b59",
      "name": "Fake FMCSA, DAT, and TIMOCOM Portals: 3 Cyberattacks Targeting US Logistics",
      "description": "Three distinct campaigns are actively targeting American trucking and logistics companies through digital platforms used for routine business operations. HelloFriends employs fraudulent carrier verification portals impersonating SAFER and Motus to harvest credentials, personal identification data, and fuel card information via sophisticated phishing infrastructure. NodeRemote distributes malware through fake broker documents and onboarding pages, deploying Node.js backdoors with rotating command-and-control infrastructure that maintains persistent remote access to compromised endpoints. The Fake Freight Portals campaign impersonates TIMOCOM and DAT, using malicious WebDAV shortcuts to install MeshCentral and CastleRAT remote access tools, while attempting to extract BitLocker recovery keys and weakening endpoint defenses. These campaigns exploit familiar business workflows including carrier verification, broker onboarding, and freight booking to compromise operational systems and sensitive business data.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-19T10:42:33.398000",
      "created": "2026-11-18T22:06:00.520000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
