    {
      "id": "6afeaded9de11b28a742cb61",
      "name": "Microsoft's agent-framework Hijacked on PyPI via Silent .pth Startup Hook",
      "description": "A supply chain attack targeted Microsoft's agent-framework package on PyPI, affecting versions 1.26.1 and 1.26.2 released on November 17, 2026. The attacker repacked legitimate wheels locally and injected a .pth startup hook that executes a credential stealer every time Python starts, regardless of whether the package is imported. The malicious code harvests environment variables containing Azure, AWS, GitHub, OpenAI, and other cloud credentials, reads configuration files from multiple locations, queries Azure metadata services for OAuth tokens, and exfiltrates compressed data to a webhook.site endpoint. Both versions were quarantined within 40 minutes but automated dependency bots had already begun propagating updates. The stealer targets 31 credential patterns, reads up to 80 files, and on Linux scans running processes for secrets.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-19T10:34:43.833000",
      "created": "2026-11-19T08:06:05.158000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
