    {
      "id": "6afeb20f28d6ef2c94a8c482",
      "name": "PHP2Shell Exploited by AI Agents from Day One: Inside a Credential-Harvesting Campaign",
      "description": "A credential-harvesting campaign exploited PHP2Shell vulnerabilities within days of public disclosure on October 21, 2026. The operation utilized attacker infrastructure at 206.245.153[.]56 serving as command-and-control, payload hosting, and data collection. An AI-agent system orchestrated exploitation using a custom job dispatcher with DeepSeek V4.1 endpoints, processing targets from a Shodan dataset of 68,198 hosts. The campaign compromised 404 systems across 57 countries, establishing persistence through SSH keys, webshells, cron beacons, and Dropbear tunnels. Operators exfiltrated cloud credentials, database backups, application secrets, OAuth tokens, and source code. Evidence suggests an initial-access-broker model, with attempts at financial fraud against payment platforms that failed to complete actual theft. The pattern indicates a financially motivated actor using AI-augmented operations to compress exploitation timelines from weeks to days.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-19T10:27:30.685000",
      "created": "2026-11-19T08:23:43.065000",
      "revision": 2,
