    {
      "id": "6ad71b768e708ffb59419b43",
      "name": "NetScaler intrusions chaining CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88779",
      "description": "In early October 2026, analysts investigated a compromise of a Citrix NetScaler ADC appliance running an affected 14.1 build. Attackers chained two vulnerabilities: CVE-2026-88771 (pre-authentication log-poisoning/RCE) and CVE-2026-88779 (SAML-parsing crash) to achieve root code execution. The intrusion deployed multiple persistence mechanisms including PHP web shells with cookie-based command channels, setuid shell modifications, cron entries, and boot hooks. Attackers installed TCP session managers, HTTP tunnels, and outbound reverse agents for command-and-control. A dedicated Go reconnaissance tool mapped internal infrastructure including DNS, LDAP/Active Directory, management services, and VMware vCenter systems. HA-aware persistence logic synchronized implants across appliance pairs and forced failovers. The campaign exfiltrated NetScaler configurations, historical data, and key material, demonstrating evolution from initial foothold to persistent platform for internal reconnaissance.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-19T07:01:16.958000",
      "created": "2026-10-20T07:42:46.232000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
