    {
      "id": "6afd5ef41efb879b09a69ff7",
      "name": "MCH and Caishen: supply chain poisoning pushes iOS exploits",
      "description": "On November 16, 2026, compromised third-party scripts delivered card skimmers and cryptocurrency clippers to visitors of major websites including BBC, Zoom, and CNN. An unauthorized party exploited a vulnerability in Optimizely's Experimentation product to inject malicious JavaScript, though other libraries like Kissmetrics, StorifyMe, and minute-ly were also affected. The campaign utilized an iOS exploitation toolkit branded Caishen, delivering exploits to mobile users while desktop visitors received card skimmers, cryptocurrency clippers, and page-data theft mechanisms. Infrastructure analysis revealed connections to MCH control panels and cryptocurrency energy rental storefronts, with over 140 instances of related panels observed. The operation's infrastructure went offline within hours of public disclosure on November 17, 2026, but new control panel hosts quickly emerged on alternative networks. Stolen cryptocurrency was rapidly moved through commercial services.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-18T09:56:38.369000",
      "created": "2026-11-18T08:16:52.723000",
      "revision": 2,
