    {
      "id": "6afcabb1c963ba9d1ae92e1a",
      "name": "URGENT: iOS Exploits Are Being Actively Deployed via Poisoned JavaScript on BBC, Zoom, CNN and Other Major Websites",
      "description": "Research reveals that threat actors have compromised third-party JavaScript providers including Optimizely, Kissmetrics, StorifyMe, and Minute-ly to deliver iOS exploits through at least 21 major websites. The attack routes Mobile Safari users to Coruna and DarkSword exploit-kit infrastructure without any user interaction. Affected sites span multiple sectors including BBC, CNN, Fox News, Zoom, GitLab, and Salesforce. Instead of targeting website backends directly, attackers poisoned widely-used analytics and content provider scripts, which then loaded malicious payloads that executed zero-click exploit chains. The compromised scripts operated via hidden iframes, leaving no visible indicators while exploiting vulnerabilities in Mobile Safari. This supply-chain attack bypasses traditional security measures as the malicious code originates from legitimate, trusted infrastructure that enterprise filters cannot block without disrupting business operations.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-18T09:37:16.419000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T19:32:01.613000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
