    {
      "id": "6afd5a8a1dc37870181386de",
      "name": "Hackers Exploit Critical ScreenConnect Flaw to Silently Run Malware on MSP Technicians' Computers",
      "description": "Attackers are exploiting CVE-2026-84869, a critical vulnerability in ScreenConnect with a CVSS score of 9.9, to execute malicious files on managed service provider technician workstations without user confirmation. The flaw allows malicious guests to send files during remote support sessions and trigger execution with elevated privileges. In a documented November 12 incident, attackers installed a rogue remote access client in approximately nine seconds. Researchers identified over 688,000 delivery attempts across 42 MSP servers between October and November, originating from 29 IP addresses. The attack chain involves batch scripts, PowerShell commands, and installation of disguised ScreenConnect clients connecting to attacker-controlled infrastructure. Affected organizations must update technician clients to version 26.6.5 or later and investigate suspicious file transfers and executions.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-18T07:59:38.975000",
      "created": "2026-11-18T07:58:02.864000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
