    {
      "id": "6afc6f47b1a4561557f1a652",
      "name": "Amazon job offer promises $5,000 a month, but it has got all the signs of a scam",
      "description": "Multiple fraudulent websites are advertising fake remote assistant positions using Amazon-like branding and domain names, promising up to $5,000 monthly. These sites, registered between July and October through the same registrar, collect personal information including names, addresses, and employment history through forms. Despite advertising remote work, applications ask about vehicle access and package delivery capabilities, indicating potential reshipping or parcel-mule fraud schemes. The operations target job seekers looking for flexible work during Amazon's legitimate holiday hiring season. Sites use identical icons and connected infrastructure, with domains like amzssapplication[.]com and applyamazonsp[.]com. Victims risk identity theft, involvement in fraud operations using stolen payment details, and financial losses through fake check schemes.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-18T07:52:15.613000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T15:14:15.837000",
