    {
      "id": "6ad5b2c95417d4d1ac959070",
      "name": "Plex vulnerabilities being exploited in the wild to drop a cryptominer",
      "description": "Multiple Plex Media Server vulnerabilities announced in September 2026 are being actively exploited to deploy cryptominers and proxy software. The exploitation chains together four CVEs to achieve remote code execution on vulnerable Plex servers. A honeypot deployment captured exploitation attempts from multiple IP addresses starting October 17, 2026. Attackers deployed XMRig cryptominer and myawesomeproxy software on compromised systems. The proxy tool potentially enables threat actors to utilize residential IPs for accessing corporate VPNs and email systems. Exploitation was observed from IP addresses 45.194.92.222, 91.92.40.202, and 176.65.139.228, with malicious payloads downloaded from 217.60.194.116. The vulnerabilities affect Plex Media Server version 1.43.2 and earlier, with proof-of-concept code publicly available through the plex2shell project.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-18T06:02:54.332000",
      "created": "2026-10-19T06:03:53.643000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
