    {
      "id": "6ad5e7f75d4f869db2238e26",
      "name": "ConnectWise (SkyKick) Vendor Credentials Abused in M365 Attacks",
      "description": "A Microsoft 365 API credential belonging to ConnectWise Cloud Backup (formerly SkyKick) was compromised and used to gain unauthorized access to customer M365 environments. The threat actor authenticated from IP address 144.172.64.128 on October 15, obtaining Microsoft Graph access tokens across hundreds of tenants. The attacker moved through tenants in sorted GUID order, suggesting automated targeting. In one instance, the ConnectWise Cloud Management MS Teams application elevated itself to Global Administrator and added credentials to other applications, including security tools. The activity began with password spraying against law firms on October 13-14, followed by role assignments in approximately 50 tenants, and culminated in widespread credential abuse. Nearly 1,000 Entra tenants showed sign-in activity from the malicious IP, with over 300 successful authentications. A second targeted wave focused on 16 tenants in policy, national security, trade, and critical mineral sectors.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-18T00:03:54.440000",
      "created": "2026-10-19T09:50:47.025000",
      "revision": 3,
      "tlp": "white",
