    {
      "id": "6afc3385bd07f5708d823e2b",
      "name": "Operation ShadowCloud: initial infection and the GitDoor backdoor",
      "description": "A sophisticated cyber intrusion campaign dubbed Operation ShadowCloud has been identified targeting government entities across Asia and Africa. Adversaries deploy two novel backdoors, GitDoor and GraphDoor, through the legitimate MeshAgent utility. These implants conceal command-and-control communications by leveraging cloud platforms including Microsoft SharePoint, GitHub, and Ably messaging services, effectively evading network detection mechanisms. The modular toolset supports on-demand plug-in downloads and in-memory shellcode injection, enabling capabilities such as keylogging, screen capture, credential theft, and proxy deployment. The operation employs DLL sideloading techniques with legitimate executables to deliver malicious loaders that decrypt and execute encrypted payloads. Multiple GitHub repositories, created since late 2024, serve as infrastructure for data exfiltration and command distribution. The campaign demonstrates advanced obfuscation including control flow flattening and multi-stage ...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T11:24:56.772000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T10:59:17.006000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
