    {
      "id": "6afc33d9e7e1114ef258bdbf",
      "name": "World's Largest Brands Infected With Malware Via Optimizely",
      "description": "On 16 November 2026, malicious JavaScript was distributed to 178 organizations through the Optimizely Web experimentation platform, affecting major sites including Zoom, BBC, CNN, Salesforce, GitLab, IKEA, and HSBC. The multi-purpose malware swapped cryptocurrency wallet addresses, skimmed payment cards, stole cookies and screenshots, and deployed Coruna and DarkSword iOS exploit kits targeting iPhones and iPads. Attackers injected their code into customer Project JavaScript fields within Optimizely snippets, which were then served from trusted cdn.optimizely.com domains. Verified cryptocurrency theft totaling approximately $7,040 occurred within nine hours, with funds moved to exchanges. The payload was rebuilt 26 times throughout the day, adding features including card skimming capabilities. Most malicious code was removed by 21:52 UTC, though Content Security Policy protections could have prevented the attack on properly configured sites.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T11:23:42.613000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T11:00:41.080000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
