    {
      "id": "6afc3457e63a03d90d550932",
      "name": "XaocMail ClickFix Campaign Drops Phantom53 and HavoX Across Latin America, Asia, and Europe",
      "description": "A Russian-speaking threat actor operates a sophisticated multi-stage campaign utilizing XaocMail phishing platform, Phantom53 DNS-over-HTTPS command-and-control framework, and Havoc post-exploitation toolkit. The operation leverages Cloudflare Workers infrastructure and ClickFix social engineering lures to deliver malicious MSI payloads. Phantom53 implements stealthy beaconing through public DNS-over-HTTPS resolvers, employs a week-keyed SHA256 domain generation algorithm for resilience, and uses scheduled tasks with Python virtual environments for persistence. The campaign shows evidence of AI-assisted development using Claude Code for automated testing and rapid iteration. Targets span Latin America, particularly Brazil and Peru, followed by entities in Asia and Europe across technology, finance, education, government, logistics, and manufacturing sectors. The attackers demonstrate advanced operational security through legitimate infrastructure abuse, reflective code loading, and sophisticated anti-sandb...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T11:19:09.897000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T11:02:47.481000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
