    {
      "id": "6afc357e27807e81d0a64eef",
      "name": "Detected Exploitation of CVE-2026-90436 against Atlassian Confluence Data Center, N-able N-central also Exploited",
      "description": "On November 6, 2026, the Apache Software Foundation disclosed CVE-2026-90436, a critical unsafe reflection vulnerability in Apache Axis 1.x that enables unauthenticated remote code execution. The vulnerability affects certain versions of Atlassian Confluence Data Center and N-able N-central when configured with non-default settings. Active exploitation in the wild was detected on November 13, 2026, targeting both products. Affected Confluence versions range from 1.x through 9.x when Remote API is enabled, while N-central requires Legacy API to be active for exploitation. Apache Axis 1.x has reached end of life with no official patches planned. Organizations must apply emergency patches or disable vulnerable APIs immediately, prioritizing internet-accessible instances and investigating exposed systems for compromise indicators.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T11:10:22.266000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T11:07:42.279000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
