    {
      "id": "6afaf0c9e29d3b2008243c83",
      "name": "Typosquatters Copy Big Brands' New Domains Within a Day of Registration",
      "description": "An ongoing typosquatting campaign has been targeting clients of brand-protection registrars CSC and MarkMonitor by monitoring their new domain registrations. Malicious actors registered 25 lookalike domains using one-character modifications within 24 hours of authentic domains being registered. The campaign targeted major brands including Abbott Laboratories, Bayer, CarMax, McDonald's, Procter & Gamble, and Sanofi. Most authentic domains were designed for marketing campaigns like patient-savings programs, sweepstakes, and legal settlements. The lookalike domains served parked pages, deceptive search portals, and brand-themed blogs containing advertisements routing visitors to scam sites. Registration occurred through China-based registrars Cloud Yuqu LLC and Chengdu West Dimension Digital Technology. Activity continues with new lookalikes detected as recently as November 11, 2026.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T10:38:18.624000",
      "created": "2026-11-16T12:02:17.890000",
      "revision": 2,
