    {
      "id": "6afb71630acda8057ec487b6",
      "name": "CVE-2026-84869 in ScreenConnect Exploited to Run Malicious Files on MSP Technician Accounts",
      "description": "A critical vulnerability in ConnectWise ScreenConnect (CVE-2026-84869, CVSS 9.9) allows malicious guests in remote sessions to push files to technician workstations and execute them with elevated privileges without authorization. Between October and November 2026, attackers conducted a massive spray campaign across 42 MSP ScreenConnect servers, issuing 688,000 malicious file-transfer requests. One successful exploitation achieved full compromise in nine seconds, deploying a rogue ScreenConnect client branded as Windows Update and connected to attacker infrastructure at masterdarky[.]com. Attack techniques included worm-like propagation, path traversal to inject startup scripts, and strategic targeting of MSP technician workstations that hold RMM consoles and customer credentials. Additional campaigns planted unauthorized crypto-exchange-named guest sessions as lures, while test runs used canary files to verify exploitation success before deploying actual payloads.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T10:06:00.591000",
      "created": "2026-11-16T21:10:59.930000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
