    {
      "id": "6afbacf0488bbec09c3d11ed",
      "name": "High volume phishing campaign uses Microsoft 365 outage lures to target multiple industry sectors",
      "description": "On November 13, 2026, a coordinated high-volume phishing campaign targeted organizations worldwide across multiple sectors. Threat actors disguised emails as legitimate Microsoft 365 service-health notifications, claiming emails were held during a service disruption and would be deleted within 24 hours unless recipients took action. The campaign used specific sender domains including moments-notice[.]com, planetmaison[.]com, and newbooker[.]com, with randomized outage subjects and recipient-specific tracking links leading to reallifeaccounting[.]com. The activity was assessed as credential phishing, though no credential capture, malware delivery, or post-compromise activity was directly observed. Microsoft Defender blocks malicious domains used in this campaign, and Defender for Office 365 quarantines phishing emails.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T10:04:03.654000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T01:25:04.092000",
      "revision": 2,
