    {
      "id": "6afbb52bb532a8221df13dd9",
      "name": "Fake crypto-wallet downloads used to deploy ScreenConnect remote access software",
      "description": "A sophisticated attack campaign is targeting cryptocurrency users, particularly those utilizing hardware wallets. The attackers employ deceptive ZIP files containing malicious BAT scripts, masquerading as legitimate wallet updates for Coldcard, Ledger, Pera Algorand Wallet, Revolut, and Xaman. The primary objective is deploying ConnectWise ScreenConnect, a legitimate remote-support application, which grants attackers complete remote access to compromised devices. Once installed, the ScreenConnect client connects to attacker-controlled infrastructure at fjksdjfdtitive[.]net on TCP port 8041, enabling command execution, data exfiltration, and potential theft of cryptocurrency credentials, wallet recovery phrases, and private keys. Affected users must immediately isolate their devices, block malicious domains and IPs, remove ScreenConnect installations, reset all credentials from clean devices, and consider moving cryptocurrency assets to new wallets generated on uncompromised systems.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T09:53:55.409000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T02:00:11.716000",
      "revision": 2,
