    {
      "id": "6afc0d22dddc5e2e49356d47",
      "name": "Beyond Optimizely: Malicious Scripts Traced Across Four Web Services",
      "description": "An investigation documents malicious JavaScript delivered through four web services: Optimizely, Kissmetrics, StorifyMe, and minute-ly. Optimizely confirmed attackers exploited a vulnerability in its Experimentation signup workflow to inject malicious code into customer projects, affecting 188 snippets across 178 organizations including BBC, Zoom, GitLab, HSBC UAE, CNN, Fox News, Salesforce, Equifax, and Ledger. Archived evidence shows poisoned responses began November 13, 2026, before the main November 16 wave. The malicious code substituted cryptocurrency addresses, monitored card details in accessible forms, and established a mobile delivery path linked to Coruna and DarkSword operations. Later-stage iOS modules targeted keychain databases and private keys, though successful exploitation remains unproven. The shared infrastructure used routing channel 02111110 and collection domains at 1688360[.]cc and webshell[.]lol. Optimizely patched the vulnerability and removed injected code, but access paths for t...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-17T09:39:05.757000",
      "created": "2026-11-17T08:15:30.078000",
      "revision": 2,
