    {
      "id": "6af7941347ca65a70dfca476",
      "name": "SCKit abuses ScreenConnect to deploy remote access and target technician sessions",
      "description": "Beginning November 11, 2026, threat actors gained unauthorized access to cloud-hosted ConnectWise ScreenConnect instances belonging to managed service providers. The attackers abuse ScreenConnect, a legitimate remote-support application, to install unauthorized remote-access clients and deploy SCKit, a malicious worm, on customer-managed endpoints. The toolkit establishes persistence through scheduled tasks and registry entries, deploying RelayTrap to deliver malicious payloads to connecting technicians. SCKit targets IT support technician workstations using hijacked authenticated ScreenConnect sessions and uses victim management consoles to distribute payloads to other managed devices. The attack chain includes PowerShell decoders, encrypted bundles using device-specific key material, and browser-access components targeting authenticated ScreenConnect sessions. The worm's deployment enables threat actors to remotely administer affected endpoints, execute commands, and deploy additional tools independently...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-16T10:51:58.579000",
