    {
      "id": "6afab9d57e1e0bda6f30aa7e",
      "name": "Analysis of NodeLinkRAT, a New North Korea-Linked RAT Abusing Public Note Services as C2",
      "description": "Between September 12 and 18, 2026, a threat actor impersonating a South Korean National Assembly aide conducted spearphishing attacks against seminar attendees using honorarium payment forms as lures. The attacker deliberately omitted attachments in initial emails to elicit victim replies, then delivered malicious LNK files through webmail. The multistage fileless attack chain involved obfuscated PowerShell scripts, free web hosting, and abuse of aNotepad as a command channel. The actor dynamically changed payloads by updating public note page contents, deploying XenoRAT, information collection scripts, document exfiltration tools, and ultimately NodeLinkRAT—a JavaScript-based remote access tool running on legitimate Node.js runtime. Exfiltration channels rotated among Dropbox, MEGA cloud, and free hosting services. The campaign employed living-off-the-land techniques, polymorphic scripts, and legitimate infrastructure abuse to evade detection while conducting cyberespionage operations targeting South Kore...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-16T10:49:20.111000",
      "created": "2026-11-16T08:07:49.687000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Kimsuky",
