    {
      "id": "6af85913b204d5d844397582",
      "name": "Threat Overview of ARTEX Autonomous Penetration Testing Framework",
      "description": "ARTEX is an open-source, large language model-driven autonomous penetration testing framework that threat actors have weaponized to automate cyber intrusions from reconnaissance through data exfiltration. Since August 2026, various malicious actors have used ARTEX to conduct global campaigns across multiple sectors, significantly reducing intrusion timeframes with some attacks progressing from initial targeting to privileged access in under three hours. Notable incidents include attacks against South Korean financial institutions affecting approximately 67,000 individuals and a supply chain compromise of ConnectWise Cloud Backup impacting over 2,250 downstream customers. Despite the original developer removing the GitHub repository in October 2026, ARTEX continues to proliferate through community forks, archived copies, and a commercial version. The framework enables threat actors with minimal technical expertise to conduct complex, multi-target operations simultaneously at machine speed, fundamentally acc...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-16T10:45:50.262000",
      "created": "2026-11-14T12:50:27.509000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Storm-3358",
