    {
      "id": "6af754d99146a92e2897881f",
      "name": "TypoPrompting: From AI Typos to Malware",
      "description": "Attackers leveraged 186 typosquatting domains across 27 AI brands including Claude, ChatGPT, DeepSeek, Perplexity, Midjourney, and ElevenLabs to distribute malicious payloads. Simple typing mistakes lead users to ClickFix lures executing hidden PowerShell commands, Microsoft Store-signed browser-hijacking applications, or search-hijacking extensions. One Claude typo delivered commands from decimal-encoded IP addresses, while others served Net Guard, a Store-signed application containing browser control capabilities. Additional routes deployed search-hijacking extensions affecting 972,000 users. The infrastructure spans 211 entry domains including lookalikes of banks, insurers, and enterprise software, with traffic distribution systems profiling visitors before serving platform-specific lures. This TypoPrompting pattern exploits legitimate workflow interruptions, turning routine AI tool access into malware delivery opportunities through parked domains and sophisticated redirect chains.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-16T10:08:38.677000",
      "created": "2026-11-13T18:20:09.275000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
