    {
      "id": "6af718eb6d8fdb6cdc927201",
      "name": "56 AWS API calls in 141 milliseconds: Inside an AI-run intrusion",
      "description": "Between September 30 and October 16, 2026, a CyberStrikeAI server executed a sophisticated AWS intrusion spanning four accounts using eight compromised identities. The attack featured machine-speed credential harvesting, with one role executing 56 EC2 user data requests in just 141 milliseconds. The adversary systematically validated stolen credentials, extracted secrets from Secrets Manager, pulled EC2 user data scripts containing sensitive information, and executed remote commands via SSM SendCommand. The attack displayed automated tooling characteristics with intermittent activity across 16 days, including a deliberate 14-day gap that evaded time-based correlation rules. All 78 alerts generated were medium or low severity individually, becoming significant only when correlated by source IP. The intrusion originated from infrastructure in Hong Kong associated with the open-source CyberStrikeAI offensive security platform.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-16T10:05:49.675000",
      "created": "2026-11-13T14:04:27.156000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "CyberStrikeAI",
