    {
      "id": "6ad2ca008bd3199ee7bb0b83",
      "name": "CVE-2026-88771: Inside the Exploitation of a Critical NetScaler RCE Vulnerability",
      "description": "On September 27, 2026, Citrix disclosed CVE-2026-88771, a critical remote code execution vulnerability affecting NetScaler Application Delivery Controller and NetScaler Gateway with a CVSS score of 9.8. The vulnerability enables unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary commands without requiring optional features. CISA added it to the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog following confirmed worldwide exploitation. Attackers employ a staged exploitation chain involving access-log poisoning, where malicious Base64-encoded payloads are staged in HTTP User-Agent headers, followed by authentication log poisoning using forged PPE failure messages containing shell commands. A vulnerable Perl diagnostic script then executes the poisoned commands with elevated privileges. Observed activities include web shell deployment, PHP enablement, and delivery of FreeBSD implants from infrastructure overlapping with CVE-2026-75650 exploitation targeting Adobe Commerce systems.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-16T01:00:51.272000",
      "created": "2026-10-17T01:06:08.544000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
