    {
      "id": "6ad1023b92a010044f3dcbc8",
      "name": "KGB RAT: A Fully Undetectable Windows Trojan Built to Spy, Steal, and Terrorize",
      "description": "KGB RAT is a Windows Remote Access Trojan actively promoted on underground forums since late 2025, marketed deceptively as a legitimate administration tool. Sold through a Malware-as-a-Service model with pricing from $150 to $800, it features credential theft, keylogging, hidden desktop takeover, ransomware capabilities, and psychological harassment functions including screamers and forced blue screens. The tool ships with a built-in FUD crypter updated daily to evade Windows Defender, requires no port forwarding for C2 connectivity, and delivers Telegram-based notifications. Evidence suggests development began in early 2022. Based on NjRAT foundation, it targets multiple operators sharing a common builder, with at least one deployment featuring an active CryptoClipper module for cryptocurrency wallet address swapping.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-14T16:03:36.356000",
      "created": "2026-10-15T16:41:31.104000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
