    {
      "id": "6ad0e1520be4762ce91fe695",
      "name": "Inside a PaperCut Attacker's AI Toolkit: Agent Instructions, Exploit Code, a Second RCE, and Victims Across 45+ Countries",
      "description": "Three exposed directories on infrastructure at 45.142.193[.]132 revealed an AI-orchestrated campaign targeting PaperCut NG/MF print management software. The exposed workbench contained AI-agent instructions, exploit code, operational logs, and post-exploitation tooling. Attackers exploited CVE-2026-81578 and CVE-2026-82078 through a Tapestry vulnerability chain, and developed a second RCE path via XML-RPC API abuse. The campaign deployed automated exploitation at scale using hundreds of AI agents running through OpenAI Codex and DeepSeek models. Post-exploitation activity included Windows credential harvesting, LSA secret extraction, reverse SOCKS5 pivoting using chisel, Metasploit automation, and Active Directory domain compromise. The actor's files documented 1,005 hosts across 45 countries in their reconnaissance pool, with 46 confirmed Active Directory domain compromises and 45 targets maintaining live internal access pivots at time of discovery.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-14T14:00:03.785000",
      "created": "2026-10-15T14:21:06.175000",
