    {
      "id": "6ad0096119a185c9dcb055b0",
      "name": "PEERSTITCH, a Stealthy FortiGate Implant",
      "description": "A sophisticated multi-stage network intrusion against a telecommunications organization in September 2024 exploited CVE-2024-47575 on a FortiManager appliance, exfiltrating configurations and cryptographic material for over 500 managed FortiGate firewalls. Attackers then exploited CVE-2025-61624 to deploy PEERSTITCH, a novel memory-resident ARM64 malware that leaves no disk artifacts or network traces. The implant operates by patching running processes, creating covert inter-process communication channels between system daemons, and intercepting network traffic. Additional attack vectors included weaponizing Apache mod_md for reverse shell command and control, impersonating the FortiManager platform to compromise downstream devices, and deploying extensive anti-forensic measures. The intrusion demonstrates advanced tradecraft consistent with nation-state actors, highlighting the critical risk of centralized edge management platforms.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-13T22:03:58.861000",
      "created": "2026-10-14T22:59:45.099000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "CL-STA-0954",
