    {
      "id": "6acf2be335dd8bbd4e27ec2e",
      "name": "2026 Q3 Linux SSH Server Targeted Malware Statistics Report",
      "description": "During Q3 2026, honeypot monitoring revealed attacks targeting poorly managed Linux SSH servers through brute force and dictionary attacks. Primary malware families included ShellBot (also known as PerlBot), a Perl-based DDoS bot with C&C infrastructure at specific IPs, and Fisieredoor, a backdoor capable of executing commands and deploying SSH dictionary attack tools. Attackers downloaded malware using wget or curl, then installed user-mode rootkits, XHide process masking tools, and XMRig cryptocurrency miners. The launcher malware utilized ld.so.preload to inject rootkits and disguised mining processes as legitimate bash sessions. Fisieredoor deployed additional tools including goauto and tsm for credential harvesting and lateral movement, transmitting successful authentication results to command servers.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-13T07:02:15.306000",
      "created": "2026-10-14T07:14:43.021000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
