    {
      "id": "6acf2be17afb8c6c6b066bc9",
      "name": "Q3 2026 Statistical Report on Malware Targeting Windows Database Servers",
      "description": "During the third quarter of 2026, attackers targeted MS-SQL and MySQL servers on Windows systems through multiple attack vectors including brute-force attacks, dictionary attacks, and vulnerability exploitation. Threat actors deployed XMRig cryptocurrency miners, GotoHTTP backdoors, and SoftEther VPN infrastructure along with various web shells including Sharp4WebCmd, Suo5, and PowerShell-based shells for persistence. Additional tools used included VShell for remote command execution, HackBrowserData for credential theft, Fscan for network reconnaissance, and Cloudflared for port exposure. Attackers created backdoor accounts for RDP access and operated SoftEther VPN servers in Cascade Connection mode as command and control infrastructure. The attacks primarily resulted from weak passwords, improper account management, and inadequate security measures on externally exposed database servers.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-13T07:02:15.306000",
      "created": "2026-10-14T07:14:41.505000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
