    {
      "id": "6acf2b317368c1ddc08ce818",
      "name": "2026 Third Quarter Windows Web Server Targeted Malware Statistics Report",
      "description": "This analysis examines attacks against Windows web servers during Q3 2026, focusing on Internet Information Services (IIS) and Apache Tomcat environments. Attackers exploited unpatched vulnerabilities, misconfigurations, and weak management practices to gain control through webshell uploads, remote code execution, proxy tools, and privilege escalation utilities. Two prominent attack cases involving CVE-2019-18935 in Telerik UI for ASP.NET AJAX are detailed. The first case deployed reverse shells connecting to 206.82.6.22, utilized Potato-family privilege escalation tools like SweetPotato and PrintSpoofer to obtain SYSTEM privileges, and installed Godzilla-style memory webshells. The second case leveraged the same vulnerability to deploy a Rust-based scanner that identified WordPress installations and reported findings via Telegram. Attackers subsequently conducted coin mining, established VPN servers, and maintained persistent remote access. Recommendations include applying current patches, minimizing exte...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-13T07:02:15.306000",
      "created": "2026-10-14T07:11:45.249000",
      "revision": 2,
