    {
      "id": "6acf002e7c7fddeb927af2d8",
      "name": "Statistical Report on Malware Targeting Linux SSH Servers in the Third Quarter of 2026",
      "description": "During the third quarter of 2026, multiple attack campaigns targeted poorly managed Linux SSH servers using brute force, dictionary attacks, and vulnerability exploits. Threat actors deployed ShellBot, a Perl-based DDoS bot, utilizing C&C servers at specific IP addresses with capabilities including port scanning and UDP flooding. A sophisticated attack chain involved launcher malware that executed user-mode rootkit libSSL2.3.0.So via /etc/ld.so.preload, subsequently deploying XMRig cryptocurrency miner disguised as -bash using XHide process concealment tool. Additionally, Fisieredoor backdoor was deployed, capable of command execution and installing SSH brute-force tools including goauto and tsm-family, which systematically targeted systems using credential lists. Organizations must implement strong password policies, regular patching schedules, and access controls for externally exposed SSH infrastructure.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-13T04:03:31.402000",
      "created": "2026-10-14T04:08:14.770000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
