    {
      "id": "6af5a58a01f1f0317453e3f6",
      "name": "How AI Revived a Stalled Attack on a U.S. Retailer",
      "description": "In September 2026, attackers targeting a U.S. retail organization initially struggled with hand-typed commands that contained errors and were blocked by security software. The following day, their tactics dramatically shifted to using AI-generated PowerShell scripts characterized by error-free code, labeled output sections, and reasoning comments typical of large language models. This AI assistance enabled rapid exploitation within minutes, including credential harvesting from SolarWinds Orion software and lateral movement to additional servers. The attackers demonstrated financially motivated objectives by searching point-of-sale scripts for passwords and credentials. Infrastructure overlaps linked this intrusion to previous attacks in August and July 2026 that showed no AI assistance, suggesting AI capabilities were recently added to existing toolkits. Similar AI-assisted attacks proliferated across multiple sectors and countries throughout 2026, with activity significantly increasing in September.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-12T16:45:48.711000",
      "created": "2026-11-12T11:39:54.659000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
