    {
      "id": "6af5c9723703485eb3ab2b49",
      "name": "PHP2Shell Exploitation on Check Point Gateway",
      "description": "In late October 2026, approximately one week after security fixes became available, attackers exploited vulnerable Mobile Access portals on Security Gateways, targeting Israeli organizations from IP address 130.94.19[.]204. The exploitation leveraged PHP2Shell vulnerabilities to gain initial access, followed by privilege escalation to root level. Attackers deployed PHP webshells for persistence, then installed TSGA malware and TSProxy backdoor components. The campaign expanded with lateral movement to VMware ESXi infrastructure, culminating in deployment of the destroy_v6 wiper and a politically-themed ransom rejection note. A second scanning wave on November 2nd targeted additional organizations worldwide without sector-specific focus, suggesting opportunistic access attempts. The toolset shows links to PhiliKit malware family and Chinese-nexus actors, though attribution remains ambiguous.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-12T16:44:29.849000",
      "created": "2026-11-12T14:13:06.174000",
      "revision": 2,
