    {
      "id": "6af5e214a7ab22c3761899ed",
      "name": "ScreenConnect Attack: SCKit Turns Remote Support Into an Attack Platform",
      "description": "On November 11, 2026, widespread unauthorized ScreenConnect deployments were detected originating from legitimate cloud-hosted management instances. The investigation uncovered SCKit, a malicious toolkit designed to abuse ScreenConnect's remote management functionality. SCKit combines rogue remote access installations with attempts to compromise technicians through a Guest-to-Host file execution technique targeting CVE-2026-84869. The toolkit's RelayTrap component attempts to reverse normal support connections by replacing legitimate ScreenConnect Guest processes and sending malicious payloads to connecting technicians. Follow-on components seek to recover .ASPXAUTH cookies from technician browsers and reuse their management permissions to distribute commands across additional endpoints. Testing confirmed the attempt but found that current patched ScreenConnect Host clients successfully blocked the reverse execution. The campaign particularly threatens MSP environments where compromised technician sessions...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-12T16:41:05.386000",
      "created": "2026-11-12T15:58:12.283000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
