    {
      "id": "6af4a92c87b5f26c33791714",
      "name": "The XG Files: Falcon C2 Flying Under The (Browser) Radar",
      "description": "A sophisticated command and control framework named Falcon (also known as XG or Xiàng Gē) has been identified operating entirely within browser contexts through malicious JavaScript. The framework compromises webmail portals and government web applications, enabling attackers to sideload malicious Chrome and Firefox extensions that steal passwords, emails, session cookies, and communications. Falcon also delivers an implant called Antino, which uses Microsoft OneDrive as a C2 channel. Between March and May 2026, government entities in one Middle Eastern country and four Southeast Asian countries were compromised, specifically targeting ministries of foreign affairs, defense, interior, and law enforcement agencies. The framework shares significant overlap with PeckBirdy and demonstrates advanced capabilities including browser proxy functionality, download interception, network traffic hijacking, and credential harvesting. The deployment suggests strategic intelligence collection objectives against governmen...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
