    {
      "id": "6af52586b68571a7151ac421",
      "name": "SCKit Worm Installs Rogue ScreenConnect Clients and Session Cookie Relays Across Hundreds of Endpoints",
      "description": "On November 11, 2026, operators exploited cloud-hosted ScreenConnect panels to deploy attacker-controlled clients and the SCKit toolkit across 288 hosts in 48 organizations. ConnectWise disabled five third-party extensions as a precaution but had not identified the initial access vector. The attack involved two stages: spreading from infected endpoints to technician workstations via session cookie theft, then laterally to other accessible endpoints. SCKit consists of 16 PowerShell and batch scripts delivered as encrypted payloads, using system UUIDs as decryption keys. The toolkit installs rogue ScreenConnect clients, creates persistence mechanisms through scheduled tasks, and attempts console takeover. While endpoint infections succeeded, the technician workstation compromise functionality failed in all observed cases. The worm includes sophisticated features like browser cookie extraction, session replay, and automated payload distribution through ScreenConnect's Shared Toolbox.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-12T10:03:21.235000",
      "created": "2026-11-12T02:33:42.753000",
