    {
      "id": "6af46b3b47e5158053c05be0",
      "name": "Off the Rails: Inside an Exposed Silent Lynx Server",
      "description": "An exposed open directory belonging to Silent Lynx, a Central Asia-focused espionage cluster, revealed the group's operations through October 2026. The directory contained tooling, data from active intrusions into government and critical infrastructure, and an AI agent used by the operator. The operator maintained persistent access to transport networks, collected government correspondence at scale including defence-related documents, and compromised a government geospatial platform. Implants matched known Laplas and Chvost families, alongside unreported variants. Lures impersonating Turkmenistan Railways were prepared for an upcoming campaign. A self-hosted AI agent running DeepSeek handled reconnaissance, collection and log cleanup. The operator worked in Russian with test traffic originating from residential Kazakhtelecom connections, supporting a Kazakhstan nexus assessment. Multiple OPSEC failures exposed the operation including storing everything on one server and leaving developer paths in binaries.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-11T16:07:52.678000",
      "created": "2026-11-11T13:18:51.949000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "YoroTrooper",
