    {
      "id": "6accfc98a21fbfce518cceaa",
      "name": "From WhatsApp to SYSTEM: Inside the VulcanRAT207.A Intrusion Chain",
      "description": "A sophisticated multi-stage intrusion chain begins with a WhatsApp-delivered financial document lure carrying Statement.exe. The malware employs NRV2E compression to conceal its true payload, which performs extensive host screening before attempting privilege elevation via COM-based techniques. Using PoolParty Variant 7 injection, the loader transfers execution into the Windows Task Scheduler process under LocalSystem authority. A downloader shellcode retrieves a compound bundle from a remote server, which deploys through a reflective loader. The deployment stage utilizes a signed GoFly driver to terminate Baidu security processes, establishes persistence via DLL side-loading with a legitimate Intel-signed VulkanInfo executable, and launches a WebSocket-based remote access trojan. The final VulcanRAT207.A payload provides extensive surveillance capabilities including shell access, keystroke capture, desktop control, network filtering, and process injection, while maintaining persistence through SYSTEM-leve...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-11T15:00:31.127000",
      "created": "2026-10-12T15:28:24.114000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "TA4922",
