    {
      "id": "6af43b7618f6962a478a6835",
      "name": "Analysis of Wpcdoor Attack Case Distributed Through Domestic DVR Management Software",
      "description": "A South Korean company's DVR management software (CMS) was exploited to distribute the Wpcdoor backdoor malware. The attack chain begins when CMS.exe installs rs.win32.exe along with a malicious IPHLPAPI.DLL file that loads via DLL side-loading. This first-stage downloader retrieves WpcMon.exe and samcli.dll, which acts as a second-stage downloader executing the Wpcdoor backdoor in memory. Wpcdoor exfiltrates system information including screenshots, clipboard data, browser credentials, wallet extension data, and supports various commands for remote control. The backdoor targets cryptocurrency wallets including MetaMask, Coinbase, and Phantom. The attacker, designated as Larva-26013, continues to deploy Wpcdoor through multiple attack vectors beyond the DVR software compromise.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-11T10:05:06.511000",
      "created": "2026-11-11T09:55:02.458000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
