    {
      "id": "6af32ca0532e5bb3ad1eb242",
      "name": "Not All That Glitters Is Gold: Tracking CopperDragon's Sparrow Framework Around the Globe",
      "description": "Over the past year, researchers investigated intrusion campaigns targeting high-profile organizations across Latin America, Asia, and Europe. These initially appeared independent but were linked through shared tools and infrastructure to the Sparrow malware ecosystem. CopperDragon is tracked as a digital quartermaster supporting China-nexus threat actors using the Sparrow cross-platform framework. Three distinct activity clusters were identified: SilentDelivery using watering-hole attacks with fake certificate warnings deploying SquadC backdoor; OceanGate targeting government and critical infrastructure with AnnobinDoor and SparrowShell backdoors; and DarkWire focusing on telecommunications and government entities using CopperDoor and CopperDNS backdoors. Operations employed sophisticated techniques including kernel rootkits, passive backdoors with packet interception, trojanized SSH tools, and extensive credential harvesting across Linux and Windows environments.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-11T09:28:59.438000",
      "created": "2026-11-10T14:39:28.302000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "CopperDragon",
      "indicators": [
