    {
      "id": "6af1ef5821afddb68d6df42b",
      "name": "Inside an AhsayCBS Intrusion: Hidden Webshells, a CryptoMiner, and a C2 Implant",
      "description": "Between October 8 and 11, 2026, threat actors exploited authentication bypass and remote code execution vulnerabilities in AhsayCBS backup management software to compromise multiple servers. The intrusion involved deploying five distinct webshell families with varying capabilities, including command execution, file operations, and encrypted payload loaders hidden in PNG images. Attackers installed two XMRig cryptocurrency miners with scheduled task persistence, staged tunneling tools, and deployed a custom Python-based implant with environmental keying that communicated with command-and-control infrastructure. The operators created Microsoft Defender exclusions, accessed backup credentials through Veeam database queries, and specifically targeted backup infrastructure to potentially access stored credentials for hypervisors and domain accounts. The sophisticated multi-stage attack demonstrated significant operational patience beyond typical smash-and-grab cryptomining campaigns.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T11:11:56.879000",
      "created": "2026-11-09T16:05:44.828000",
      "revision": 3,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
        {
          "id": 4179025578,
          "indicator": "creepexplosiondarknight.com",
