    {
      "id": "6af22c7231935985c957ec55",
      "name": "Trusted by Default: Qubole Cross-Account Access Abused in the Wild",
      "description": "A threat actor exploited IAM credentials from Qubole's AWS account (805246085872) to assume integration roles in customer environments between October 14 and October 26, 2026. The attacker used two IAM users and multiple VPN addresses to gain access, then conducted extensive reconnaissance across affected AWS accounts. Activities included enumerating storage, databases, and identity resources, harvesting credentials from Lambda environment variables, Secrets Manager, and SSM Parameter Store, and validating discovered credentials using TruffleHog. The actor exfiltrated data from S3 buckets opportunistically, downloading whatever each assumed role could access. A suspicious bootable Linux ISO image was also identified, designed for remote deployment and system reconnaissance. The campaign appears opportunistic rather than state-sponsored, exploiting trusted cross-account relationships that remained active despite many integrations being unused.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T11:10:05.025000",
      "created": "2026-11-09T20:26:26.261000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
