    {
      "id": "6af22c74c56e69bb42cb8363",
      "name": "On the hunt for ARTEX: understanding agentic attacks in AWS environments",
      "description": "In October 2026, an AI-native penetration framework called ARTEX was observed conducting attacks against AWS environments, primarily targeting financial data. ARTEX operates through LLM agents that autonomously plan and execute attacks based on operator-defined objectives. Observed activity included exploitation of compromised long-term IAM access keys to search CloudWatch logs for financial information, file paths, and secrets. Additionally, attackers abused public Amazon Cognito user pools through anonymous sign-ups, token collection, and AWS account enumeration. Datadog identified hundreds of internet-exposed ARTEX consoles, often in Mandarin and hosted in Singapore and Hong Kong. The framework has been linked to China-aligned threat actor Storm-0940 and demonstrates sophisticated post-exploitation capabilities including automated resource discovery and credential harvesting across cloud environments.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T11:08:01.731000",
      "created": "2026-11-09T20:26:28.512000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Storm-0940",
