    {
      "id": "6af22c723959134a2c8d25fa",
      "name": "Malicious bee-js npm Release and Swarm Desktop Releases Deliver SleepyDuck Ethereum C2 Backdoor",
      "description": "On November 9, 2026, threat actors compromised Ethersphere's release pipeline through two compromised GitHub accounts, publishing malicious @ethersphere/bee-js 13.3.0 to npm and trojanized Swarm Desktop 0.56.2 releases. Both artifacts contained loaders fetching JavaScript from api[.]frameworkmetrics[.]xyz with full Node.js privileges. The infrastructure, including Ethereum smart contract 0xf8a900Db50b3331be6B768bA460BB59f3E40C344 for C2 addressing, matches SleepyDuck/EtherDuck operations from October 2026 targeting Open VSX extensions. The malicious npm package ran through legitimate trusted publishing workflows with valid SLSA provenance, while Swarm Desktop releases were signed with Apple Developer ID and notarized. Payloads exfiltrated Bee node passwords and wallet keys, then deployed Go backdoors on macOS/Linux and ScreenConnect remote access tools on Windows, specifically targeting developers working with Ethereum tooling.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T09:24:22.612000",
