    {
      "id": "6af2d6b5777af782c0ecd03b",
      "name": "Contagious Interview - One Interview Away From Infection",
      "description": "A sophisticated campaign targeting software developers through fake job interviews has been exposed, using a fraudulent company called AccuraSoftHire as a front. The operation lures developers through legitimate job platforms like Indeed and Glassdoor, with recruiters using identity-verified LinkedIn profiles. Candidates receive take-home coding assignments containing malicious npm packages disguised as Tailwind CSS plugins. When built, these packages deploy loaders that fetch additional payloads from remote servers using blockchain dead drops. The company's career site also serves a fake camera driver that delivers the same malware. This attack vector, linked to previous North Korean campaigns, has infected tens of thousands of machines globally and resulted in significant cryptocurrency theft, including the Binance breach exceeding six billion dollars.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T09:18:43.945000",
      "created": "2026-11-10T08:32:53.603000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
