    {
      "id": "6af1c04bc9cb5773cc15b8bc",
      "name": "The Industry Leader in Enterprise Brand Protection",
      "description": "A sophisticated phishing campaign has been identified targeting hospitality customers through fake hotel reservation pages impersonating Booking.com and other hotel services. The operation uses personalized reservation details including hotel names, dates, prices, guest information, and contact details to enhance credibility. Two main visual templates share the same underlying codebase: one closely mimics Booking.com while another uses generic Best Hotel Reservation branding. The kit employs advanced features including real-time card validation using Luhn checksums, interactive verification workflows, multi-language support spanning Japanese, Chinese, Korean, European languages and others, and three backend endpoints for tracking victim progression. Pages continue interaction after initial card submission through polling mechanisms that can present additional verification prompts. The campaign shows particular focus on Japanese hotels but is designed for global deployment across multiple countries and curr...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T09:04:10.936000",
      "created": "2026-11-09T12:44:59.049000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
