    {
      "id": "6af1bfe0945ca03e48243de3",
      "name": "Shai-Hulud Descendant Surfaces in Malicious Ruby Gem That Steals Credentials and Poisons AI Tools",
      "description": "A malicious Ruby gem, strutil-core version 1.0.1, executes a 5.48 MB credential-stealing worm during installation. Published on November 1, 2026, by RubyGems account jamnajiea, the package was flagged 70 seconds after release and removed within five hours. The payload, a new build of the testmetest worm from the Miasma family descended from the Shai-Hulud toolkit, steals credentials from cloud services, CI systems, package registries, SSH, AI coding tools, and cryptocurrency wallets. It propagates through RubyGems, npm, PyPI, JFrog Artifactory, GitHub, GitLab, and SSH. The worm installs a Python backdoor controlled via signed GitHub commits, poisons AI tool configurations to maintain persistence, and includes a conditional wiper that deletes the user's home directory when a stolen GitHub token is revoked. The malware targets Linux and macOS systems on x86-64 and ARM64 architectures, excluding Russian-speaking locales.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-10T09:03:48.838000",
      "created": "2026-11-09T12:43:12.759000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
