    {
      "id": "6ac8a46214e2077a0bfe7409",
      "name": "NEBULA: Seven Fake AI SDK Packages on npm Install a Windows RAT That Needs No DLL",
      "description": "In late September 2026, an actor deployed seven malicious npm packages masquerading as a NebulaAI software development kit to deliver a Windows remote-access trojan. The operation, tracked as NEBULA, spans four sequential burner accounts (nebulallms through nebulallms4), with api-nebula and llm-nebula remaining downloadable. Each package presents a convincing AI client facade while hiding an obfuscated installation hook executing malicious logic. The underlying RAT operates exclusively through direct NT and win32k syscalls, bypassing standard DLL imports with an empty Import Address Table. Features include hidden-desktop remote control (HVNC), Kernel Streaming for camera and microphone monitoring, and Winlogon Shell persistence. The payload is a customized KNTRAT variant communicating with 65.87.7.132 using user-agent kntrat/0xB15B00B6. The implant masquerades as conhost.exe and suppressed beaconing during analysis, consistent with embedded anti-analysis provisions.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-08T08:03:54.747000",
      "created": "2026-10-09T08:22:58.387000",
      "revision": 2,
