    {
      "id": "6aedb6e052da4a432861b11c",
      "name": "Inside Help TDS: Hotejka, Cloudflare Pages and Predictive Detection",
      "description": "Infoblox attributes the Help Traffic Distribution System (TDS) to Hotejka, a small Russian-language affiliate program believed to be a rebrand of ROI777, which was exposed in 2018. Operating since April 2017, this TDS delivers tech support scams directing users to call centers where social engineering convinces victims to install remote desktop tools like UltraViewer, enabling persistent access for malicious activities. Hotejka's affiliates include Balada Injector, Detour Dog, and DollyWay, who redirect traffic through compromised websites, malvertising, social media, and spam. Since April 2026, operations have leveraged free Cloudflare Pages infrastructure, creating approximately 300 new domains daily. Infoblox developed predictive detection capabilities that identify malicious domains seven days before deployment, successfully detecting over 16,000 domains and reducing customer exposure from 4% to 0.5%. The scam employs browser locks with alarming warnings impersonating Microsoft, ultimately leading vict...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T19:07:52.169000",
      "created": "2026-11-06T11:15:44.015000",
      "revision": 2,
