    {
      "id": "6aedb6df481d077141e5e5e4",
      "name": "Remcos RAT",
      "description": "This intelligence analysis details a malicious campaign involving Remcos RAT, a commercially available remote access trojan. The attack chain begins with a weaponized Excel spreadsheet (Remittance Advice.xlsm) that executes VBA macros. Upon opening, PowerShell retrieves remote scripts (edi.vbs/firewall.vbs) from a malicious domain. The execution progresses through multiple stages, ultimately deploying the Remcos RAT payload. Command and control infrastructure utilizes domains at dvrlists[.]com and lbl[.]support. The threat demonstrates typical social engineering tactics using financial-themed lures to entice victims into enabling macros and initiating the infection chain.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T18:59:55.886000",
      "created": "2026-11-06T11:15:43.551000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
