    {
      "id": "6aed32c8b1c53b811aaa8bb0",
      "name": "A Dish Served Lukewarm: The Refrigerator Botnet",
      "description": "Exposed Dixell/Copeland XWEB PRO refrigeration controllers are being exploited as abuse infrastructure. The STRIKE Team discovered a suspected SMTP botnet comprising nine IP addresses, with three confirmed as refrigeration controllers. These devices, used in supermarkets and cold storage facilities, remain exposed on the internet with unpatched vulnerabilities, particularly CVE-2026-25085. Attackers are repurposing these controllers as tunnel gateways, residential-proxy exits, and spam senders. Analysis revealed outbound-only SMTP traffic with significant target-list overlap among nodes, indicating coordinated operations. Of 1,041 mail targets, 508 were hit by multiple nodes, with the three most active sharing approximately 47% of their targets. The exposed controllers carry vulnerable firmware and lack security monitoring, making them ideal for prolonged malicious use without detection.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T10:46:18.670000",
      "created": "2026-11-06T01:52:08.470000",
      "revision": 3,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
