    {
      "id": "6aed89b36eddd48d6b209367",
      "name": "ARTEX: Agentic Asbestos",
      "description": "ARTEX is an open-source, LLM-driven autonomous penetration testing framework released in July 2026 that integrates AI agents with reconnaissance and exploitation capabilities. As of November 2026, 1,465 hosts run exposed ARTEX consoles globally, with approximately 815 distinct deployments. CrowdStrike linked ARTEX usage to attacks against South Korean financial institutions, while Microsoft attributed its use to Storm-0940's ConnectWise supply chain compromise. The framework enables automated operations from reconnaissance through data exfiltration with minimal human intervention. Ten percent of ARTEX hosts also run other offensive tools including Cobalt Strike, Vshell, and additional AI attack frameworks. Operators frequently expose open directories containing exploit binaries, post-exploitation kits, and session histories. The tool's developer claimed it was intended for authorized testing and took the repository offline after public attribution, though archived copies remain circulating.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T10:46:14.322000",
      "created": "2026-11-06T08:02:59.514000",
      "revision": 3,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Storm-0940",
