    {
      "id": "6aeceaf8cfe0e0287c9a54a1",
      "name": "Email threat landscape: Q3 2026 trends and insights",
      "description": "From July through September 2026, approximately 7.3 billion email-based phishing threats were detected, with September reaching nearly 3 billion attacks—a 41% increase from August. The quarter demonstrated significant shifts in attack techniques, including a sharp decline in QR code phishing, a recovery in CAPTCHA-gated attacks driven by SVG attachments, and persistent domain spoofing affecting 129 million messages impersonating business services. Credential theft remained the dominant objective across malicious attachments, while business contact impersonation declined and Teams-based threats increasingly used ordinary personal names rather than explicit help desk identities. Notable campaigns targeted legal organizations with personalized salary review lures leading to device code phishing, and Spanish-speaking users with purchase order and payroll themes delivering Agent Tesla malware. The disruption of Tycoon2FA phishing platform continued showing effectiveness with 99.8% volume reduction.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T10:45:27.092000",
      "created": "2026-11-05T20:45:44.580000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
