    {
      "id": "6ac5f1632c72bc95740deede",
      "name": "Attackers Target AI Development Platform Langflow",
      "description": "In September 2026, F5 Labs detected 405 exploitation attempts targeting CVE-2026-0768, an unauthenticated remote code execution vulnerability in Langflow AI application-building platform, originating from 55 distinct IP addresses. This marks the first observation of an AI/ML development platform RCE in opportunistic internet-wide scanning. Captured payloads included capability probing with unique markers, timing-based execution checks, and environment harvesting attempts aimed at extracting cloud credentials, model API keys, and database secrets. Activity came primarily from two infrastructure clusters: Google Cloud hosts using environment-harvesting payloads with forged AI-crawler User-Agents, and European scanning subnets employing marker-based capability probing with spoofed localhost headers. The vulnerability, disclosed in January 2026, allows Python code injection through decorator and default-argument evaluation on the validation endpoint without authentication, enabling arbitrary code execution wit...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-06T07:03:30.159000",
      "created": "2026-10-07T07:14:43.871000",
      "revision": 2,
