    {
      "id": "6aec6059b2260af9dd811d39",
      "name": "Inside Phexia: A macOS malware delivered through ClickFix",
      "description": "Phexia is a modular macOS backdoor and infostealer actively distributed through ClickFix campaigns since late 2025. The malware employs a multi-stage infection chain beginning with Terminal command execution that downloads shell scripts, establishes persistence via LaunchAgents, and deploys AppleScript-based loaders. A significant evolution occurred in May 2026 when operators began using Polygon blockchain smart contracts as command-and-control dead-drop resolvers, replacing earlier Telegram and Steam-based methods. Post-compromise activities include credential harvesting through fake password prompts, browser data theft, keychain extraction, password manager targeting, and XMRig cryptominer deployment. The malware collects login passwords, browser encryption keys, cookies, and cryptocurrency wallet information. Multiple distinct builds communicate with rotating infrastructure, with reinfection potentially leaving concurrent installations active on compromised endpoints.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-05T20:30:34.998000",
      "created": "2026-11-05T10:54:17.581000",
      "revision": 2,
