    {
      "id": "6aec5fe933b8cac0f8ed7334",
      "name": "Supply chain attack: BO Team in a software developer's infrastructure",
      "description": "In June 2025, a software developer detected suspicious SMB connection attempts, revealing a sophisticated compromise by the Black Owl (BO Team) APT group. Attackers seized nearly all infrastructure components including domain controllers, servers, virtual environments, Ansible orchestration, backups, and security systems. They exploited CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell) on VMware vCenter, compromised hypervisors using stolen SSH keys, and infiltrated both Windows and Linux infrastructures through credential theft and brute-force attacks. Evidence suggests attackers aimed to inject malicious code into the developer's software products to enable supply chain attacks against customers. The attackers maintained persistent access for several months using custom backdoors, but the operation was detected before completion, preventing potential widespread compromise of downstream organizations.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-05T20:27:31.610000",
      "created": "2026-11-05T10:52:25.634000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Black Owl (BO Team",
