    {
      "id": "6aec5fe9d7ff10f7065a9f18",
      "name": "How to detect fileless attacks exploiting ToolShell: analyzing the Storm-2603 incident",
      "description": "In 2025, threat actors exploited CVE-2025-53770 and CVE-2025-53771 (ToolShell vulnerabilities) in on-premises Microsoft SharePoint to achieve remote code execution. Storm-2603 deployed ransomware following successful exploitation. Analysis of a December incident revealed attackers using the IIS worker process as an in-memory bridge, maintaining access entirely within w3wp.exe without writing to disk. The intrusion occurred in two stages: initial vulnerability fingerprinting on December 20, followed by full exploitation on December 24. The attackers deployed a fileless webshell framework with multiple modules for reconnaissance, privilege escalation via token impersonation, and persistence. Post-exploitation activities included deploying Velociraptor for command execution, establishing multiple tunneling mechanisms, attempting to kill EDR solutions using vulnerable drivers, and deploying Warlock ransomware.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-05T20:22:38.713000",
      "created": "2026-11-05T10:52:25.006000",
      "revision": 3,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Storm-2603",
      "indicators": [
