    {
      "id": "6aec39f1c741f78d03f95337",
      "name": "Grand Theft Auto VI Release Phishing Lures",
      "description": "Ahead of the highly anticipated Grand Theft Auto VI release on November 19, 2026, threat actors are exploiting consumer hype through phishing campaigns and fraudulent schemes. Analysis of 121 newly registered domains containing 'cyberleek' and other GTA VI-themed domains revealed four primary lure categories: fake downloads impersonating popular leaker CyberLeek, false early access offers, nonexistent mobile versions, and free game promises. These malicious sites distribute trojans, request cryptocurrency payments, employ content lockers that require survey completion for affiliate revenue, and harvest personal information. Tactics include fake storefronts impersonating developer Rockstar, fraudulent APK files requiring unsafe installation permissions, and giveaway scams using urgency counters. Post-launch threats are expected to shift toward in-game currency fraud, credential phishing for Rockstar and gaming platform accounts, and malware distribution through fake cheats and modifications.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-05T09:57:42.292000",
      "created": "2026-11-05T08:10:25.498000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
