    {
      "id": "6aeb9ec5f0df7c45eb2cdd32",
      "name": "SkyW4lker Phishing Kit: Microsoft 365 Threat to US Firms",
      "description": "SkyW4lker is an active device-code phishing kit targeting Microsoft 365 users primarily in the United States, Europe, and other regions. By exploiting Microsoft's legitimate authentication process, attackers gain access to corporate accounts without stealing passwords or bypassing MFA. Between June and October 2026, 618 sandbox analyses identified related activity, with submissions increasing from 20 in June to 200 in September. The United States accounts for 47% of submissions, with organizations in technology, manufacturing, and government sectors most affected. The kit uses phishing emails with password-protected attachments containing links that lead victims through CAPTCHA pages to Microsoft's authentication system. Technical analysis reveals obfuscated JavaScript, IP-based geolocation, and polling mechanisms. SkyW4lker shares infrastructure and code modules with the Gabagool credential phishing kit, suggesting both were developed by the same actor.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-05T09:57:12.306000",
      "created": "2026-11-04T21:08:21.079000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
