    {
      "id": "6aec3e073e76c608aeccf05d",
      "name": "Summary of Malicious Program Distribution via Goddess of Victory: NIKKE PC Launcher",
      "description": "Level Infinite disclosed that the PC launcher for the game \"Goddess of Victory: NIKKE\" was compromised when four script files on the official CDN were tampered with between September 27 and November 4, 2026. The modified scripts downloaded a remote access agent (internally named K2F) that could execute arbitrary commands, steal credentials from browsers, cryptocurrency wallets, and cloud services. The malware persisted by injecting a DLL into Chrome and could intercept wallet recovery phrases. The compromise began with domain hijacking of insightjs.com on September 27, with script tampering occurring shortly after. Malicious payload distribution to users started October 30. Level Infinite detected the anomaly on November 4, replaced compromised files, and deployed automated detection and removal functionality on November 5. Users who launched the Windows PC launcher between September 27 and November 4 were potentially affected.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-05T09:37:28.951000",
      "created": "2026-11-05T08:27:50.807000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
