    {
      "id": "6ae9a41c3b21a1b31d13d6b6",
      "name": "DarkBlinders: Active Espionage Campaign",
      "description": "A sophisticated cyberespionage operation targeting Israel and the Kurdistan Region of Iraq was conducted by DarkBlinders, the threat actor behind the Blinder Tunnel campaign. Active between August and October 2026, the campaign compromised a high-profile Israeli individual associated with the security sector and a government cloud environment in the Kurdistan Region. The operation employed government webmail, cloud-drive, and meeting-service lures, including phishing infrastructure impersonating the Gulf Cooperation Council Secretariat General and Kuwait's Ministry of Foreign Affairs. GitHub repositories under the PeakyBlindersTeam account served as command-and-control infrastructure. The attackers used selective activation, reviewing metadata from infected hosts before deploying a second-stage backdoor enabling PowerShell command execution. Post-compromise activity included credential theft and exfiltration of at least 1 GB of data from the government cloud environment. The activity demonstrates connectio...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-05T09:22:43.370000",
      "created": "2026-11-03T09:06:36.542000",
