    {
      "id": "6aeb62d591162af275e93f90",
      "name": "ARTEX Exposed: Infrastructure Behind the South Korea Bank Hack",
      "description": "Between late September and early October 2026, seven South Korean financial institutions experienced breaches affecting approximately 66,000 individuals and 2,200 corporations. The intrusions were attributed to ARTEX, an AI-driven autonomous penetration testing framework. Investigation revealed exposed infrastructure at 38.244.50[.]120 and 23.248.226[.]250, uncovering AI model-routing components, custom Claude Code skills, proxy management utilities, and exploitation tooling. The operation utilized DeepSeek, GLM, and Grok models through the xcai[.]pro reseller domain. Recovered artifacts included FOFA reconnaissance tools, JNDI/LDAP exploitation chains, Linux privilege escalation exploits, cryptocurrency-exchange access scripts, and mobile-device utilities. The infrastructure spanned multiple countries with 1,303 distinct IP addresses identified through certificate, malware classification, and HTTP title hunting methods.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-04T19:42:06.502000",
      "created": "2026-11-04T16:52:37.775000",
      "revision": 2,
