    {
      "id": "6aeb242105ebdc46e55850e9",
      "name": "From Business Emails to XLoader: An Order Lure That Led to In-Memory Injection",
      "description": "Morphisec has observed increased XLoader activity using business-themed email lures. The attack chain begins with order confirmation or payment request emails containing RAR archives that hold obfuscated JScript files. When executed, the JScript extracts an x86 LuaJIT interpreter and Lua loader to the user's Documents directory. The Lua loader attempts security interference, decodes an embedded packed PE, and manually maps it into LuaJIT memory. The packer then decrypts the XLoader core and executes it within the same thread. XLoader creates a clone of itself and uses shared-section injection to map into a selected x86 target process, redirecting thread execution context. The final payload implements credential stealing capabilities including Windows Vault enumeration and cookie extraction, while communicating with 16 configured C2 endpoints. Additional payloads delivered in this campaign include Agent Tesla, Remcos, and XWorm.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-04T19:01:46.500000",
      "created": "2026-11-04T12:25:05.823000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
