    {
      "id": "6aeb242026030af6a32b4b10",
      "name": "Poisoned Source: APT29 Watering Holes Targets Mobile Devices",
      "description": "Sekoia TDR identified a large-scale watering hole campaign employing three infection vectors: compromised legitimate websites, Adversary-in-the-Middle-like impersonating high-profile domains, and supply-chain compromise of Ukrainian Plerdy analytics service. The injected JavaScript code profiles browser and device attributes before delivering platform-specific n-day exploit chains targeting iOS or Android devices. Exploited vulnerabilities include CVE-2025-43529, CVE-2024-27834, CVE-2026-20700, CVE-2025-14174, CVE-2025-43510, CVE-2025-43520, CVE-2026-3910, and CVE-2025-27038. Final payloads exfiltrate browser cookies, Wi-Fi passwords, and comprehensive device data without persistence, consistent with intelligence-gathering objectives enabling session hijacking and access to browser-based services. Based on technical overlaps, operational patterns, victimology and infrastructure analysis, this campaign is attributed with moderate-to-high confidence to APT29, a Russian nexus intrusion set widely linked to th...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
