    {
      "id": "6aea24c415c16b64650d5689",
      "name": "Fake-download campaign uses trojanized installers to deliver monetization payloads",
      "description": "Microsoft Threat Intelligence identified an evolving campaign targeting users searching for cracked commercial software, free games, activators, and unofficial utilities. The operation uses trojanized Inno Setup-style installers to distribute multiple monetized software payloads through a per-offer callback and status-tracking system. Three downstream monetization branches transform affected devices into monetized assets: routing third-party internet traffic through the device via WorldProxyPool, enrolling devices in distributed-computing platforms through CharityEngine and BOINC, or installing utility-style software such as Advanced Windows Manager. These components are silently installed through deceptive software bundles without informed user consent, introducing security and privacy risks. The campaign employs a four-stage attack chain progressing from deceptive lures through Inno-based staging, offer-controlled payload delivery, and installation of monetization branches using scheduled tasks for persi...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-04T08:29:38.745000",
      "created": "2026-11-03T18:15:32.173000",
      "revision": 2,
