    {
      "id": "6aea271df4897a00b60de744",
      "name": "Gorbag: Orcs at the border harvesting intelligence from Ukraine",
      "description": "A Russia-aligned threat actor named Gorbag has been operating since February 2025, conducting highly targeted cyberespionage operations against Ukrainian organizations. The group primarily focuses on law enforcement, justice entities, local administrations near the front line, and the defense sector. Rather than establishing long-term access, Gorbag employs simple infostealers for rapid intelligence collection, harvesting browser credentials, VPN configurations, and selected documents in single-pass operations. The group's toolset includes Prime ReverseShell (a PowerShell reverse shell) and BeautyStealer (a C++ browser-data and file stealer). Initial compromise occurs through spearphishing emails with malicious attachments. In early 2026, Gorbag updated its attack chain to exploit CVE-2025-8088, a WinRAR path traversal vulnerability. The operational focus on quick data collection suggests Gorbag may function as an initial access broker, sharing collected credentials with other Russia-aligned threat actors ...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-04T08:29:18.899000",
      "created": "2026-11-03T18:25:33.589000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Gorbag",
