    {
      "id": "6ae9eb17c5d87b8a004ed8fb",
      "name": "StyleSmuggler Exploitation Deploys PSK Agent RAT Against Magento Stores",
      "description": "Between September 9 and September 13, 2026, a coordinated campaign exploited Magento and Adobe Commerce stores across Western Europe, North America, and Asia-Pacific using CVE-2026-75650 (StyleSmuggler). The attack chain delivered a shell-script dropper, PSK Agent RAT, and PHP webshell through the /paypal/transparent/response/ endpoint. The dropper achieved 0% detection on VirusTotal at time of analysis. The campaign deployed chi_down, a 10.5 MB obfuscated Go binary with remote access capabilities including command execution, SOCKS5 proxying, and encrypted communications. DNS exfiltration was used to track successful compromises. Chinese-language comments in the dropper and infrastructure naming suggest a likely Chinese-speaking operator, though attribution to a specific threat group is not supported. Multiple operators are exploiting the same vulnerability with distinct toolkits.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-03T16:28:06.136000",
      "created": "2026-11-03T14:09:27.567000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
