    {
      "id": "6ae9ac6e66c89c6be4d99928",
      "name": "Exploitation Targeting Node-RED, a Tool Embedded in ICS Products",
      "description": "On October 30, 2026, exploitation activity was detected targeting CVE-2026-58115, an unauthenticated Node-RED admin API vulnerability. Attackers deployed malicious flows that automatically download and execute Linux bots through three layers of encoding. The exploit originated from IP 4.201.105.116 in Microsoft's network and utilized Node-RED's inject and exec nodes to execute commands without authentication. The dropper retrieved binaries from 85.215.73.250:8080, saving them to RAM-backed storage at /dev/shm/.b to avoid disk forensics. Multiple payload variants were observed, including staged shell scripts and persistent webshells. The activity demonstrates opportunistic mass scanning across multiple CVEs rather than targeted operations. Node-RED is embedded in critical infrastructure products including Siemens SIMATIC IoT2050 devices, making this vulnerability particularly significant for industrial control systems environments.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-03T09:50:57.777000",
      "created": "2026-11-03T09:42:06.626000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
