    {
      "id": "6ae9a05a6c8de6ce3516b3c8",
      "name": "The Internals of a Badbox Operation",
      "description": "Investigation reveals a massive supply chain compromise involving MECOOL Android set-top boxes manufactured by Videostrong Technology Co., Ltd. Over 1.3 million devices were pre-infected with the x.cpe backdoor, granting operators system-level access through MQTT infrastructure. The backdoor deploys multiple payloads including residential proxy SDKs and ad fraud modules like AdMoyu, Appsalt, APSolo, LinkFog, and Gaganode. Approximately 500,000 devices remain actively online, predominantly affecting Malaysia, Mexico, and Brazil. The operation functions as a pay-per-install campaign fueling ad fraud and proxy ecosystems. Google has permanently banned Videostrong from the Android ecosystem following these findings. Investigation conducted in partnership with Motion Picture Association, Google, Plume, Trend Micro, Lumen, and HUMAN Security.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-03T08:56:01.210000",
      "created": "2026-11-03T08:50:34.200000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Videostrong Technology Co., Ltd.",
