    {
      "id": "6ae38be9be54297cf156f922",
      "name": "SEO Poisoning Campaign Targets DeepSeek Users: Chinese Threat Actor Deploys Kong RAT via Multi-Stage Attacks",
      "description": "A sophisticated SEO poisoning campaign targets users searching for DeepSeek AI tools through malicious lookalike domains positioned on first-page search results. The attack employs a multi-stage infection chain beginning with weaponized MSI files disguised as legitimate DeepSeek software. The execution flow progresses through multiple stages involving shellcode, DLL side-loading via legitimate Cyglaunch software, and ultimately deploys Kong RAT. The threat actor registered domains mimicking DeepSeek and distributed ZIP archives containing code-signed fake installers to add legitimacy. Attribution points to a potential Chinese threat actor based on PDB paths referencing '52pojie', a Chinese cybersecurity forum. This campaign appears to be a continuation of previous operations from April 2026 targeting users of Chinese developer tools including FinalShell SSH client, Xshell, and Clash proxy. The final payload includes keylogger functionality and establishes persistence through registry modifications.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-03T07:44:48.925000",
      "created": "2026-10-29T18:09:45.562000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
