    {
      "id": "6ae8a86845dfd06f55cb0848",
      "name": "Shutting the Door on the XCPE Botnet",
      "description": "Google and industry partners dismantled the XCPE backdoor that enrolled over 1.3 million set-top boxes into a botnet. The backdoor was intentionally developed and operated by Videostrong Technology Co., an Android OEM/ODM, who monetized it by selling access to criminal affiliates. These affiliates loaded malware modules conducting ad-fraud, enrolling devices into residential proxy networks, and installing additional malware. The disruption also severed access to at least 10 million additional compromised devices by taking down affiliate C2 domains. The malicious software was built directly into various device models over multiple years with dedicated infrastructure. Google has banned Videostrong from making certified Android devices and implemented improvements to firmware integrity reviews on Android TV devices.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-02T23:28:30.417000",
      "created": "2026-11-02T15:12:40.194000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Videostrong Technology Co.",
