    {
      "id": "6ae86a19eabc583f87c50fd6",
      "name": "CyberStrikeAI attacks educational institutions",
      "description": "An open-source framework called CyberStrikeAI was used in real-world attacks against educational institutions across Africa and Latin America. The framework combines LLM-based orchestration with a traditional C2 server, where an AI model on the server plans actions and generates commands while an implant executes them on compromised hosts. Attackers initially gained access through compromised SQL Server infrastructure, then deployed the CyberStrikeAI agent which performed reconnaissance, privilege escalation, credential dumping, lateral movement, and data exfiltration. The AI orchestrator automated post-exploitation activities that traditionally require manual operator intervention, reducing the skill barrier for attackers. While the AI component operates server-side, the actual malicious activities on victim systems use standard techniques like Kerberoasting, AS-REP Roasting, LSASS dumps, DCSync, and Golden Ticket attacks, making them detectable through conventional security controls. Chinese-language art...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-02T23:18:44.087000",
      "created": "2026-11-02T10:46:49.678000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
