    {
      "id": "6ae5866df62f40be3fe5904b",
      "name": "Fake Claude Code extension in Cursor: How to find the backdoor",
      "description": "On October 29, 2026, Cursor's VS Code extension marketplace served malicious Claude Code extensions (versions 2.1.312 and 2.1.313) designed to plant SSH backdoors on developer machines. The fake extensions, not developed by Anthropic, operated for approximately 11 hours before removal. They installed attacker SSH keys, established reverse SSH tunnels to 134.209.82[.]225, and created persistence mechanisms disguised as legitimate system components. Expel investigated four incidents involving Mac computers, discovering that malicious activity occurred up to 8 hours after Cursor's stated exposure window closed. The backdoor survives extension uninstallation and requires separate removal. The attack collected system information including hostname, username, Git email, and environment variable names. Organizations relying solely on the 11-hour exposure window for scoping may miss compromised machines.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-02T23:01:39.035000",
      "created": "2026-10-31T06:10:53.454000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
