    {
      "id": "6ae5411ce86c1aaec037ddbf",
      "name": "Black October for AI Developer Platforms",
      "description": "Throughout October 2026, at least nine AI Developer Platforms experienced security breaches involving credential theft and subsequent abuse of AI model access. The attacks targeted platforms including Fireworks AI, Andromeda, Zeabur, Lightning AI, OpenCode, Railway, Warp, CommandCode, and Northflank. Attackers exploited various vulnerabilities to access stored environment variables containing AI credentials, then monetized stolen access through LLM broker infrastructure. Follow-on activity included validation sweeps, quota enumeration, and large-scale token abuse resembling resold coding-agent traffic. Two documented cases show approximately 800,000 and 1.7 million unauthorized Bedrock calls respectively, generating over $100,000 in fraudulent usage. Multiple reseller operations were identified, including actors using infrastructure at llm-routing.com and xingjiabiapi.org, selling discounted access to frontier models using stolen credentials.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-02T22:56:55.827000",
      "created": "2026-10-31T01:15:08.981000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
