    {
      "id": "6ae4c9f97b4e07a268c06b96",
      "name": "PHP2Shell One Week Later: Honeypot Shells on the Web, a Path to Root on Palo Alto Firewalls",
      "description": "PHP2Shell emerged from two critical PHP memory-safety vulnerabilities, CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619, rated CVSS 9.2 and patched on October 21, 2026. Investigation of open directories uncovered 616 PHP2Shell-related files revealing widespread exploit development across multiple operators. While exploitation succeeded only on honeypots operated by watchTowr, 0x4D31, and GreyNoise for the open internet, the vulnerability has been successfully weaponized against Palo Alto PAN-OS firewalls. Attackers chained PHP2Shell with the Fragnesia Linux kernel privilege-escalation vulnerability (CVE-2026-46300) to obtain root access on 25 PAN-OS firewalls. The campaign utilized AI-driven reconnaissance frameworks to automate target selection, narrowing approximately 19,000 internet-facing firewalls to 240 high-value targets. Multiple operator clusters were identified sharing exploit toolkits, custom heap exploits, and staging infrastructure targeting government ministries, national banks, telecommunications, and cr...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-02T22:50:10.081000",
      "created": "2026-10-30T16:46:49.009000",
      "revision": 2,
