    {
      "id": "6ae4a5754dedf6097f0cfd5d",
      "name": "Belarus-Linked Hackers Deploy Wiper Malware in First Documented Destructive Attack on Ukraine",
      "description": "Belarus-aligned threat actors deployed a VBScript wiper against a Ukrainian manufacturing company involved in the transportation sector in late May 2026. The group, tracked as FrostyNeighbor (also known as UNC1151, PUSHCHA, Storm-0257, and TA445), utilized Chisel, UltraVNC, and Cobalt Strike before delivering the destructive payload through Group Policy. This incident marks the first documented destructive cyberattack by a Belarus-aligned actor, representing a shift from traditional espionage operations. The targeted company's role in Ukraine's transportation sector suggests potential wartime operational value. Researchers assessed that Belarus-aligned groups are becoming increasingly aggressive and selecting targets aligned with Russian intelligence priorities, potentially acting as a proxy, though direct cooperation remains unconfirmed.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-11-02T22:35:29.524000",
      "created": "2026-10-30T14:11:01.621000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "FrostyNeighbor",
      "indicators": [
