    {
      "id": "6ae4564eb479948d2335e8d1",
      "name": "Polymarket Breach Alert: Wallet-Draining Code Found in a Third-Party Script",
      "description": "A malicious JavaScript file was discovered in a third-party performance monitoring integration on Polymarket. The script, hosted on a DebugBear CDN URL, contained sophisticated code designed to access authenticated trading sessions, inspect user portfolios, and transfer cryptocurrency assets to attacker-controlled addresses. The payload searches for active trading clients and signers within the user's browser session, then attempts to sell positions or transfer tokens directly. Analysis revealed code that reads authentication context from local storage, traverses React component structures to locate trading functionality, and constructs EIP-712 signed messages to move assets. A fallback recipient address embedded in the script showed holdings exceeding $2.1 million. Production build metadata from Polymarket confirms removal of the DebugBear integration. While the script's malicious capabilities are established through static analysis, the total number of victims and aggregate losses remain unverified.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-30T09:52:48.021000",
      "created": "2026-10-30T08:33:18.931000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
