    {
      "id": "6ae386434a2934ca4f48754d",
      "name": "Aurora ransomware targets ESXi abuses Cursor Agent for exploitation",
      "description": "Aurora ransomware group has been active since approximately April 2026, targeting organizations across multiple countries and operating a data leak site. The investigation revealed the group deploys a Linux ransomware variant specifically designed for ESXi environments, using ChaCha20 encryption with RSA-4096 key wrapping. A distinctive characteristic includes the abuse of Cursor Agent with Claude Sonnet AI to assist with hands-on exploitation activities across ten target organizations between April and May 2026. The AI agent performed tasks including privilege enumeration, network scanning, NTLM relay attacks, and certificate attacks. Operators imposed specific restrictions prohibiting DCSync, account lockouts, and adding new computer objects to domains. A second cluster of activity attributed to Aurora used different tactics including SQL Server lateral movement, GodPotato escalation, and S3-based exfiltration affecting eight organizations across multiple countries.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-30T08:21:47.532000",
      "created": "2026-10-29T17:45:39.286000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "aurora",
