    {
      "id": "6ae38bc5290b5bac6b7748e0",
      "name": "Investigating Abuse of Remote Desktop and Bulk Mailing Apps",
      "description": "Investigation into a tech-support scam led to discovering connections between the remote-access application UltraViewer and bulk-mailing software UltraMailer. DNS and email analysis revealed a long-running QuickBooks phishing campaign utilizing over 350 lookalike domains and tracking domain chanret[.]com. The campaign directs victims to call scammers attempting to steal QuickBooks credentials while exposing recipient information through UltraMailer tracking pixels. UltraMailer is openly promoted on criminal forums as a spamming tool with no abuse-reporting mechanism. The investigation also uncovered trojanized installers containing authentic copies of both applications, including one UltraMailer installer carrying njRAT. When the QuickBooks actor briefly switched to Mail250, the account was suspended after reporting, but the campaign resumed using UltraMailer infrastructure. While no evidence suggests developers participated in these activities, the findings demonstrate widespread criminal abuse of legitim...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-30T00:18:17.024000",
      "created": "2026-10-29T18:09:09.493000",
      "revision": 2,
