    {
      "id": "6ae346b2ba6034789081c550",
      "name": "Sandbox Flipped to 'Danger-Full-Access': Unauthorized AI Relays Create Risk for Organizations",
      "description": "An unauthorized relay service has been installing genuine OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code command-line interfaces on enterprise systems, then reconfiguring them to route all requests through third-party infrastructure. Active since early 2026, the service has impacted organizations primarily in mainland China, with additional cases in South Korea, Taiwan, and Malaysia. Affected sectors include industrial automation, electronics manufacturing, semiconductors, pharmaceuticals, and petrochemicals. The delivery mechanism uses fileless PowerShell or bash scripts fetched from lookalike domains. The reconfiguration disables execution sandboxes entirely, enables network access, replaces legitimate API credentials with relay-issued tokens, and disables telemetry. While no evidence of abuse exists, the configuration grants operators access to read every prompt, file, and secret, with commands executing under full user privileges.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-29T16:03:56.334000",
      "created": "2026-10-29T13:14:26.416000",
      "revision": 2,
