    {
      "id": "6ae346b144e7d60cfc369b7f",
      "name": "NIK C2: The new AI-enabled command-and-control framework",
      "description": "A sophisticated AI-integrated command-and-control framework named NIK C2 has been discovered, featuring a Windows implant capable of credential dumping, keystroke streaming, and real-time AI-powered data analysis through the OpenAI Chat Completions API. The Go-based implant employs dual-channel C2 architecture with TLS-secured WebSockets and HTTP fallback, utilizing AES-256-GCM encryption. It includes surveillance capabilities, lateral movement tools, screen-locking ransomware deployment demanding Bitcoin or USDT payment, and bootkit preparation features. The framework demonstrates advanced defense evasion through AMSI patching, process hollowing, and anti-debugging measures. Development spans at least three versions compiled with Go 1.23.4, indicating active evolution by a technically proficient team. Active C2 infrastructure was observed at IP 87.120.196[.]120 hosting domain total-sitevv[.]lol, confirming operational deployment beyond proof-of-concept status.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-29T16:02:25.692000",
      "created": "2026-10-29T13:14:25.921000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
