    {
      "id": "6ae0b1549b888d367073448e",
      "name": "PHP2Shell: Exploitation Attempts and Remediation Trends",
      "description": "Wiz Research has been monitoring exploitation attempts targeting two critical PHP vulnerabilities since their public disclosure on October 21, 2026. While no successful attacks have been observed in their telemetry, some private exploits have been shared that work against various targets. Telemetry shows a 67% decrease in exposed vulnerable machines and a 47.9% reduction in significantly affected organizations within one week. Observed exploitation attempts include tools using the PHP2Shell mechanism matching public proof-of-concepts, though none completed the full exploit chain. Challenges preventing successful exploitation include request-size limits, memory exhaustion failures, and difficulties with worker pinning across different PHP configurations. Additionally, some tools branded as PHP2Shell exploits actually relied on unrelated session poisoning techniques requiring separate local file inclusion vulnerabilities. Despite limited success to date, PHP2Shell remains a significant risk requiring immedia...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-29T10:49:49.517000",
      "created": "2026-10-27T14:12:36.408000",
