    {
      "id": "6ae205cefd1c69f6a9b3116d",
      "name": "68 GB Stolen From a Philippine Government Agency's Overseas-Employment Databases, Exposed by the Operator's Own Open Directory",
      "description": "An unidentified operator exfiltrated 68.837 GiB of database backups from a Philippine government agency managing overseas employment and migrant workers on 6 September 2026. The theft involved 27 SQL Server backups containing case-management systems including POEA and OFW variants. The operator inadvertently exposed their staging infrastructure via an open HTTP directory on a UpCloud VPS in Singapore, revealing a rebranded GodPotato privilege escalation tool (renamed Wrqsnx), PowerShell stagers, Impacket toolkit, and transfer logs. The payload leverages DCOM and RPC mechanisms to achieve SYSTEM-level access without exploiting vulnerabilities. Certificate analysis linked the compromised infrastructure to the Philippine Overseas Employment Administration portal farm. Initial access vectors and command-and-control channels remain unidentified, though tooling was delivered to agency portal hosts.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-28T22:14:53.163000",
      "created": "2026-10-28T14:25:18.105000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
