    {
      "id": "6ae205cd5f78e91614edbd47",
      "name": "Managed for Malice: How Attackers Turn MDM into Remote Access",
      "description": "Threat actors are weaponizing legitimate mobile device management platforms, including Hexnode and Rippling, through social engineering techniques to establish unauthorized remote access to victim systems. Attackers use phishing emails with business-themed lures, such as proposals and meeting invitations, to trick users into enrolling devices or installing management agents. Once MDM access is established, adversaries leverage this trusted, privileged path to deploy unauthorized remote monitoring and management tools like ScreenConnect, which connect to attacker-controlled relays. The deployment chain typically follows a pattern: social engineering leading to MDM enrollment, followed by RMM installation and external relay connections. This technique demonstrates the challenge of distinguishing legitimate administrative tools from malicious use, as the MDM platforms themselves are not compromised but rather misused through deception.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-28T21:51:28.418000",
      "created": "2026-10-28T14:25:17.108000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
