    {
      "id": "6ae205cc6609fd489e50c1b4",
      "name": "False Protection, Emptied Accounts: The Seven Android Trojan Families Targeting Indian Banking Apps",
      "description": "Group-IB's Threat Intelligence team uncovered a sophisticated Android malware campaign systematically targeting India's financial services sector since July 2025, orchestrated by the financially-motivated threat cluster CyberDakait. The operation distributes seven distinct malware families through coordinated smishing and vishing campaigns, impersonating bank representatives to trick victims into installing malicious APKs. These trojans harvest sensitive banking credentials, credit card details, and outstanding balances through overlay attacks while simultaneously conducting cryptojacking using XMRig. The malicious applications are hosted on GitHub repositories to maintain legitimacy, with the initial APK functioning as a dropper for the main payload and cryptocurrency mining module. Analysis revealed at least 17,960 compromised devices with 7.6 million intercepted SMS messages, including OTPs and transaction notifications. Attackers primarily target victims through fraudulent Credit Card Protection Plan s...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-28T21:50:09.596000",
      "created": "2026-10-28T14:25:16.555000",
      "revision": 2,
