    {
      "id": "6ae1b031bb4673daca05fd52",
      "name": "Malicious Firefox Extensions Impersonate Phantom, Jupiter, and Bitget to Steal Wallet Secrets",
      "description": "Three malicious Firefox extensions impersonating popular cryptocurrency wallets—Phantom, Jupiter, and Bitget—were discovered stealing recovery phrases and private keys from users. The extensions use Unicode homoglyphs to mimic legitimate wallet names and route stolen credentials to brand-named subdomains of bonto[.]io. The Phantom impersonator employs a two-stage approach: a loader fetches additional payloads from a remote server at runtime, allowing operators to modify malicious code post-review. All three extensions bundle complete stealers in signed packages that capture seed phrases, private keys, and clipboard data. The campaign uses separate throwaway developer accounts for each listing and provisions infrastructure for additional targets including Coinbase and Exodus wallets. Captured secrets grant attackers complete control over victims' cryptocurrency wallets and assets.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-28T10:37:12.029000",
      "created": "2026-10-28T08:20:01.428000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
