    {
      "id": "6ae185cf23690a9648c6f503",
      "name": "Inside Qilin ransomware: ESXi attacks, affiliate networks and double extortion",
      "description": "Qilin, also known as Agenda, is a Russian-speaking ransomware-as-a-service operation active since 2022 that became one of the most prolific groups by 2025 with over 1,000 claimed victims. The operation employs a flexible platform allowing affiliates to customize attacks targeting local files, network shares, and virtual machine infrastructure. Affiliates typically gain initial access through phishing, stolen credentials, vulnerable internet-facing systems, and remote management tools. The group follows a double-extortion model, encrypting systems while threatening to publish stolen data via their blog and WikiLeaksV2 platform. Notable incidents include the 2024 Synnovis attack affecting UK healthcare services. Qilin has been linked to Moonstone Sleet and Scattered Spider, with some operators creating derivative operations including The Gentlemen and Securotrop, the latter maintaining affiliate status while operating an independent leak site.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-28T10:20:14.266000",
      "created": "2026-10-28T05:19:11.486000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
