    {
      "id": "6ae185d0d24a85ae5c54ae6f",
      "name": "RATatouille: Today's Special: Impersonating Companies in Korea, Payments in Cryptocurrency",
      "description": "Infrastructure tracking related to ValleyRAT led to the discovery of multiple fraudulent websites impersonating legitimate Korean companies including Doosan Robotics and Cheonjeong. These sites used authentic corporate logos, videos, and descriptions to appear legitimate while offering features like invitation-code registration, VIP memberships, and cryptocurrency deposit/withdrawal functions. Online chat support provided instructions for USDT payments via TRON wallet addresses, requiring users to submit transaction screenshots. Analysis revealed TRON wallet addresses with significant transaction volumes, including one wallet that received approximately 13 million USDT cumulatively. Infrastructure analysis starting from ValleyRAT C2 IP address 14.128.53[.]155 identified 12 potentially associated domains. However, no direct operational connection has been confirmed between ValleyRAT malware operations and these fraudulent websites or cryptocurrency wallets.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-28T10:18:40.030000",
      "created": "2026-10-28T05:19:12.074000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
