    {
      "id": "6ae14ab2a51c8b2b96924ba2",
      "name": "Omegatech Is Disrupted, and the Pressure on Bulletproof Hosting Keeps Building",
      "description": "The FBI seized virtualine[.]net on October 27, 2026, under Operation Omegaline, targeting Virtualine Technologies, which operated as Omegatech (AS202412). This bulletproof hosting provider emerged in February 2026 after infrastructure shifted from Railnet LLC (AS214943). Bulletproof hosting providers rent servers to cybercriminals while ignoring abuse complaints, enabling phishing, malware, and ransomware operations. Over the past year, 50 such providers lost their autonomous system numbers due to law enforcement action, sanctions, or strategic abandonment. Despite seizures, operators quickly rebrand and acquire new ASNs within days, moving malicious IP ranges to continue operations. Recent enforcement actions include Dutch seizure of THE.Hosting servers, US charges against Russian nationals, and EU sanctions against Media Land. The investigation involved FBI Washington Field Office, Germany's Polizei Hessen, Netherlands' Politie Midden-Nederland, UK's National Crime Agency, and private partners.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-28T10:12:06.161000",
      "created": "2026-10-28T01:06:58.531000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
