    {
      "id": "6ae10d3bd4b201062c857223",
      "name": "SkyW4lker Phishing Kit: Microsoft 365 Threat to US Firms",
      "description": "SkyW4lker is an active device-code phishing kit exploiting Microsoft 365 authentication processes across the United States, Europe, and other regions. Operating since June 2026, it bypasses MFA by abusing legitimate OAuth 2.0 device-code flows, granting attackers access to corporate accounts without stealing passwords. The kit uses phishing emails with password-protected attachments containing links that lead victims through CAPTCHA pages to malicious sites requesting Microsoft device codes. Analysis revealed 618 sandbox submissions between June and October 2026, with 46% originating from US organizations. Monthly activity surged from 20 cases in June to 200 in September. Technical investigation uncovered shared infrastructure and code similarities with the Gabagool credential phishing kit, suggesting common development. The kit employs obfuscated JavaScript, IP-based geolocation, and PHP backends to track victim authentication status, primarily targeting technology, manufacturing, and government sectors.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-27T23:52:41.632000",
      "created": "2026-10-27T20:44:43.449000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
