    {
      "id": "6ae0cd6f9f3a85948233e4b9",
      "name": "Locked and Loaded: Phishing through Fake Bids and Protected Documents",
      "description": "A sophisticated credential phishing campaign leverages fake business bid invitations to target professionals. The attack begins with an email titled 'Project Bid Invitation' containing a password-protected PDF attachment that evades automated security scanning. Once opened, the PDF displays a fake OneDrive button redirecting victims to a fraudulent shared document drive. Recipients are prompted to select files for download, then asked to enter their email address, mimicking legitimate document-sharing platforms. This leads to a counterfeit Microsoft login page where entered credentials are harvested and transmitted to attacker-controlled servers. The campaign exploits trusted business processes, password protection mechanisms, and familiar brand interfaces to bypass both technical defenses and human vigilance, making it particularly effective against employees conditioned to respond urgently to legitimate business opportunities.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-27T23:26:27.819000",
      "created": "2026-10-27T16:12:31.604000",
