    {
      "id": "6ae095cebdd5fe9e0d5209f2",
      "name": "Domain Shadowing: Attackers Abuse Institutional Domains",
      "description": "Two unrelated operations exploited domain shadowing techniques to place illegal gambling content beneath legitimate educational and government domains in Bangladesh, India, and Mexico. Unauthorized parties gained access to DNS administration, creating records beneath established institutional namespaces to leverage their reputation for search engine optimization. Hidden Hawk added individual CNAME records mapping institutional hostnames to gambling pages hosted primarily on Cloudflare Pages, affecting over 850 entry points across eight domains. A separate campaign targeting Maharashtra government domains delegated entire subzones to third-party nameservers using wildcards, enabling external management of numerous hostnames. Both operations served Indonesian and Indian illegal gambling content worth an estimated $6 trillion globally in unregulated markets, exploiting institutional trust to boost search rankings and acquire traffic while leaving primary websites intact and potentially unnoticed by domain own...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-27T16:34:51.926000",
      "created": "2026-10-27T12:15:10.794000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Hidden Hawk",
