    {
      "id": "6ae095c9103f37d94d160182",
      "name": "PHP2Shell (CVE-2026-109618/9) Havoc: UNC actors leveraging Public Exploit Code Against Public, Business And Educational Infrastructure",
      "description": "Two critical use-after-free vulnerabilities in the PHP engine, CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619, rated CVSS 9.2, affect the session.upload_progress feature. These flaws trigger during multipart request parsing before application code executes, bypassing WAFs and enabling unauthenticated remote code execution. Within 48 hours of the October 21, 2026 patch release, exploit code spread rapidly across GitHub. Diverse UNC actors deployed automated scanning and exploitation tools targeting over 70% of internet-facing PHP infrastructure running unpatched versions (prior to 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36, 8.2.35). Observed campaigns include mass exploitation scripts, Mirai botnet C2 infrastructure, session poisoning chains via WordPress LFI vulnerabilities, and automated reconnaissance using proxy pools. Honeynet telemetry captured active exploitation from multiple IP addresses, demonstrating weaponization across public, educational, and business sectors globally.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-27T16:21:59.690000",
      "created": "2026-10-27T12:15:05.184000",
      "revision": 2,
