    {
      "id": "6ae095c5697cb799b2ecd396",
      "name": "How VBScript Malware Evades Detection Using Trusted Tools Copy",
      "description": "Three malware campaigns using VBScript have been identified targeting victims primarily in Brazil and Portugal through phishing attacks. The campaigns deliver Overlord RAT, Lampion trojan, and an unknown RAT using fake legal notices, financial documents, and invoice pages. Attackers employ multi-stage execution chains involving obfuscated VBScript, batch files, and DLL side-loading with legitimate Windows components like VMware network libraries and VLC player. The malware establishes persistence through scheduled tasks and registry modifications while attempting to evade detection by adding Defender exclusions and checking for virtualized environments. Infrastructure analysis reveals Brazilian-based command and control servers, with payloads delivered through cloud services including Dropbox, Google Cloud Storage, and AWS S3. The campaigns demonstrate sophisticated techniques combining social engineering, trusted application abuse, and encrypted payloads to compromise systems and maintain remote access ca...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-27T15:21:01.696000",
      "created": "2026-10-27T12:15:01.566000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
