    {
      "id": "6ade9b49eed172cd38ff41e7",
      "name": "Gheist: Attempted Scaled Abuse of Stolen GitHub Tokens Stumbles",
      "description": "Since September 15, 2026, an automated campaign named Gheist has been performing mass abuse of compromised GitHub tokens. The attack commits a workflow named sync-check to every accessible repository, designed to print repository secrets into workflow logs. These secrets are then exfiltrated through GitHub's API and the logs deleted seconds later. Over 13,500 planted branches from more than 850 compromised accounts have been recovered, affecting personal projects and enterprise private repositories. While GitHub's approval controls have blocked exploitation in public repositories, private repositories and GitHub Enterprise environments remain vulnerable. The campaign uses no command-and-control server, carries the user agent 'gheist', and has been actively evolving with multiple variants. Approximately two-thirds of implicated accounts have been removed from GitHub, likely due to response activities.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-26T11:07:48.783000",
      "created": "2026-10-26T00:14:01.366000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
