    {
      "id": "6add9cbb9d565685946f59b0",
      "name": "deepveindrilling.com: Magento CMS block loader hits 953 stores",
      "description": "A criminal group has compromised 953 online stores, predominantly Magento shops, since July 2025 by injecting malicious JavaScript loaders into CMS blocks. The latest domain, deepveindrilling.com, was registered in October 2026 and employs sophisticated bot detection using browser fingerprinting to evade security scanners. The loader stores malicious code in visitors' localStorage for persistent execution. The campaign utilizes five different domains over 15 months, previously leveraging Keitaro traffic distribution system. Attackers exploited known Magento vulnerabilities, particularly PolyShell and SessionReaper file upload flaws, to gain initial access. The final payload targets cryptocurrency users with fake Ledger wallet pages. Most compromised stores were previously infected victims that were reinfected through persistent database access and backdoors, demonstrating the attackers maintain long-term access even after initial cleanup attempts.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-26T11:03:41.872000",
      "created": "2026-10-25T06:07:55.987000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
