    {
      "id": "6adbc9083a47da5843e87e6a",
      "name": "Inside the LiteLLM 1.107.0 supply chain compromise: Credential theft through Python startup hooks",
      "description": "On October 21, 2026, LiteLLM version 1.107.0 was compromised and distributed through PyPI and official container images. The malicious package leveraged Python startup mechanisms to execute credential-stealing payloads automatically, without requiring applications to actively import LiteLLM. Attackers utilized stolen developer GitHub credentials to redirect the release workflow to a lookalike repository. The payload targeted authentication material across developer tools, AI applications, cloud environments, browsers, and infrastructure. Two execution paths were identified: a credential collector launched through path extensions and a Unix-oriented loader persisted through site-specific configuration. Collected credentials were encrypted using AES-256-CBC with RSA-wrapped keys and exfiltrated to attacker-controlled infrastructure. The compromise affected not only LiteLLM gateway deployments but also developer workstations, CI/CD agents, test systems, and containers where Python was executed in affected env...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-26T10:33:55.198000",
      "created": "2026-10-23T20:52:24.298000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Storm-0940",
      "indicators": [
        {
          "id": 4540398179,
