    {
      "id": "6ad91a62b48f2e8558fd4787",
      "name": "LiteLLM PyPI Package and Docker Images Compromised to Steal Cloud and AI Credentials",
      "description": "LiteLLM version 1.107.0 was compromised through a supply chain attack affecting both PyPI packages and Docker images. The malicious release contains Python startup files that automatically execute upon Python initialization, stealing cloud credentials, private keys, browser data, and AI development tool authentication. Socket's AI scanner detected the compromise seven minutes after publication. Container build provenance reveals the attack used a lookalike repository (Berri-AI/litellm instead of BerriAI/litellm) in the release workflow. The payload targets AWS, Azure, Google Cloud credentials, GitHub CLI, SSH keys, npm/PyPI configuration, and AI tool credentials including Claude, Gemini, and Cursor. Stolen data is encrypted and exfiltrated to a command-and-control server. A separate loader mechanism enables remote Python code execution. The package receives approximately 23 million weekly downloads, making the impact significant.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-22T10:22:52.562000",
      "created": "2026-10-21T20:02:42.318000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
