    {
      "id": "6ad857db71667a30647a5232",
      "name": "Dissection of Operation FlashHole, a complex attack by Lazarus",
      "description": "In January, Lazarus Group launched Operation FlashHole against South Korea, exploiting mandatory security software CrossWeb EX through watering hole strategies and targeted spear-phishing emails with fake portfolio and resume sites. The campaign began in July the previous year, targeting software, construction, and cable equipment manufacturing sectors. The attack chain combines old and new malware families including TechHub, Cubridge, TouchShift, TouchHub, ClientHub, and LPEClient. Notable techniques include in-memory execution, GitHub and Dropbox for command-and-control infrastructure, DLL side-loading, and the incorporation of post-quantum cryptography (ML-KEM-1024) and GOST encryption. The sophisticated modular framework demonstrates Lazarus's continuous evolution of tools and tactics specifically designed for South Korean targets.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-21T06:40:48.339000",
      "created": "2026-10-21T06:12:43.502000",
      "revision": 3,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Lazarus Group",
