    {
      "id": "6ad74f34161c4cb0598be46f",
      "name": "Swallowtail: Russian Espionage Group Targets Defense Firms in Two NATO Countries",
      "description": "Russian espionage group Swallowtail targeted organizations across two NATO member states, including a law enforcement agency, naval shipbuilder, and military aircraft engine manufacturer. During a two-month intrusion at the naval shipbuilder, attackers deployed the Hookedge backdoor delivered through malicious Word documents. They conducted hands-on-keyboard operations, stealing credentials through two distinct techniques: deploying an SSH private key to establish a persistent tunnel into the internal network, and using a PowerShell script to capture NTLM handshakes. The attackers also deployed a previously undocumented reflective loader (ld.exe) that decrypts payloads in memory using runtime-supplied keys. All targets hold information of direct interest to foreign intelligence, consistent with a broad collection effort against European government and defense sectors.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-20T14:40:00.443000",
      "created": "2026-10-20T11:23:32.078000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "APT28",
