    {
      "id": "6ad632287e9fae87583d6526",
      "name": "AOMEI Backupper update servers hijacked to push malware: Check your PC",
      "description": "Between April and July 2026, attackers compromised AOMEI Technology's update and notification infrastructure to distribute malware to users of AOMEI Backupper, backup software used by over 100 million people worldwide. During three confirmed tampering windows lasting ten, six, and five minutes, attackers modified download instructions to deliver a malicious ZIP archive containing an initial downloader that installed a persistent remote-access backdoor. The compromised infrastructure also serves AnyViewer customers. The brief tampering periods made detection difficult while limiting infection opportunities. The backdoor enables attackers to execute commands and install additional malware, leaving infected systems vulnerable to further compromise. Users can check for infection by scanning with security software, examining Task Scheduler for RadminComponentRuntime tasks, searching for unsigned upgrade-now.exe files, or monitoring suspicious network traffic to specific domains and IP addresses.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-19T15:17:55.388000",
      "created": "2026-10-19T15:07:20.711000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
