    {
      "id": "6ad220cc0811c90b23c261eb",
      "name": "QuartzLine: A working PDF viewer with a backdoor inside",
      "description": "QuartzLine, also tracked as CLOUDHAZE by Mandiant, is malicious software disguised as a functional Windows PDF viewer that conceals a backdoor enabling attackers to execute commands and deploy additional malware. The malware has appeared as paperline.exe and fielddesk.exe, signed with a legitimate but now-revoked EV code-signing certificate. Distribution occurs through malicious advertising, where users searching for unrelated content click ads and download the viewer from AWS S3 buckets. Once installed, QuartzLine establishes persistence through scheduled tasks and communicates with command-and-control infrastructure. Observed attack chains include Chrome data theft within one week of installation, followed by deployment of second-stage RATs like Caira and IronBark. The backdoor operates with user-level privileges and can execute arbitrary Windows commands.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-19T10:26:58.740000",
      "created": "2026-10-16T13:04:12.969000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
