    {
      "id": "6ad1d33960a4dd738f97701a",
      "name": "An Analysis of Suo5-Based Tunneling and Pivoting Attack Techniques Through Case Studies",
      "description": "This analysis examines exploitation of Suo5, an HTTP/HTTPS-based tunneling tool, for pivoting attacks through compromised web servers to access internal networks. Suo5 relays TCP traffic and enables SOCKS5 proxy access to internal systems, supporting multiple transmission modes and environments including Java, PHP, IIS/.NET, and Nginx. Two deployment methods were observed: file upload exploitation on IIS servers through renamed ASPX files, and memory injection via Jenkins Script Console using Groovy scripts to register Suo5 as Servlet and Filter components. Key indicators include repeated POST requests in web logs, DLL files in Temporary ASP.NET Files directories, and PluginServletFilter chains in Java logs. Detection strategies recommend monitoring web request patterns, server-side behaviors, abnormal User-Agent headers, unauthorized URI access, and file modifications in web application paths, alongside restricting script execution capabilities and implementing network segmentation controls.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-19T09:31:15.191000",
      "created": "2026-10-16T07:33:13.914000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
      "indicators": [
