    {
      "id": "6ad0c30399495ae02dc7664a",
      "name": "Aoki: Infostealer Targets AI Coding Assistant Credentials",
      "description": "The Aoki infostealer has evolved to target credentials from AI coding assistants including Claude, OpenAI's Codex, Cursor, Codeium and Gemini. This capability represents a recent addition, as earlier versions did not target AI-related files. The malware steals API keys, tokens and session files that could enable attackers to conduct activities under legitimate user identities, access connected repositories, cloud services and CI/CD pipelines. Beyond AI credentials, Aoki harvests data from dozens of browsers, cryptocurrency wallets, password managers, messaging applications, gaming platforms, VPN and FTP clients. The malware collects available data and transmits it to command-and-control servers. This development suggests AI credentials are becoming as valuable as traditional targets like payment card data and cryptocurrency wallets for cybercriminals.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-15T14:33:10.895000",
      "created": "2026-10-15T12:11:47.867000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
