    {
      "id": "6ad0c5a0a6d66a2d742e590c",
      "name": "Exposing AdFection: How Discover-Tech Turned Targeted Ads Into a Pipeline for Zero-Click Mercenary Spyware",
      "description": "This investigation reveals the first public confirmation of zero-click mercenary spyware delivered via targeted advertisements, termed AdFection. Devices at Al Jazeera were infected with Candiru spyware through malicious ads purchased by Israeli company Discover-Tech, which operates as a facilitator for mercenary spyware partners. Discover-Tech's Controlium platform enables partners to de-anonymize, fingerprint, and automatically infect devices when advertisements render. Analysis of four billion bidding records shows ads were displayed across nearly 200,000 websites and apps in dozens of countries. The company appeared on Google and IAB Europe vendor lists from 2020-2026, serving ads via major networks. Discover-Tech is linked to multiple mercenary surveillance actors including Candiru, Intelos, and Bindecy, and supports mass-deanonymization through mobile carrier vulnerability exploitation. The infrastructure also covertly directed millions of devices to contact Candiru servers for tracking and reconnais...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-15T14:31:51.161000",
      "created": "2026-10-15T12:22:56.990000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Caramel Tsunami",
