    {
      "id": "6acf8736e6d91800bcdb734a",
      "name": "Disruption Targets Major Chinese-Language Phishing Kits with Japanese Focus",
      "description": "A coordinated disruption action targeted Chinese-speaking cybercriminals operating three major phishing kits: CoGUI, CoAceV, and CoFish_Ws, which collectively distributed hundreds of millions of credential phishing messages primarily targeting Japanese organizations. These operations impersonated 66 well-known brands, mainly consumer and finance companies, to steal usernames, passwords, and payment data. The threat actors demonstrated sophisticated capabilities, utilizing approximately 17,000 unique domains with frequent rotation and evasion techniques. The ecosystem enablers YAM Store and Iron Man were also targeted through a civil lawsuit and domain seizures, conducted in collaboration between Microsoft, Health-ISAC, and multiple security partners. This coordinated action is expected to significantly impact the Chinese phishing ecosystem and cause substantial operational disruption to multiple threat groups conducting financial fraud.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-15T09:57:53.928000",
      "created": "2026-10-14T13:44:22.828000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "YAM Store",
