    {
      "id": "6acec272f01b1f0cac6ecb2a",
      "name": "Clean Install, Stolen Creds: Fake WatchGuard VPN Site Serves Genuine Signed Client",
      "description": "In early October, a sophisticated credential phishing campaign targeted WatchGuard Mobile VPN users through a fake download site at watchguard-vpn[.]net. The attack used SEO poisoning to appear in search results and deployed a unique technique: after collecting victim credentials twice through browser pop-ups, it downloaded the genuine, validly signed WatchGuard installer directly from WatchGuard's official CDN. This eliminated malicious files that security tools could detect. The first credential submission was deliberately rejected as incorrect to collect multiple passwords. The credential collection endpoint at watchguard-ssl[.]online received server addresses, usernames, and passwords, providing attackers network access. This domain was previously reported in January with no backend functionality but was re-registered in August with full phishing capabilities implemented by September.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-14T06:46:36.532000",
      "created": "2026-10-13T23:44:50.179000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Storm-2561",
      "indicators": [
