    {
      "id": "6accbe14102992eb5a52b063",
      "name": "The phone was compromised before the user turned it on: the rise of Midnight Mimosa",
      "description": "A sophisticated malware campaign targets low-cost Android devices built on MediaTek platforms, with malicious code preinstalled in device firmware before users receive them. The platform-signed system application operates with elevated privileges, enabling operators to silently install applications, grant permissions, and load remote code. The scheme primarily generates revenue through ad fraud, click fraud, device information collection, and converting infected devices into residential-proxy botnet nodes. The malicious system application ships under various system-sounding names including com.android.system.lite, com.android.sys.prot, and com.android.sys.gmsprot. Operators deploy at least 32 disguised applications including fake weather, app-lock, and OCR tools. The malware disables Google Play Store during payload installation to evade detection, then re-enables it afterward. Thirteen related applications were also discovered on Google Play, communicating with identical command-and-control infrastructure...",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-13T13:36:03.552000",
      "created": "2026-10-12T11:01:40.720000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Midnight Mimosa",
