    {
      "id": "6ac964afdcc4acb43c3ef335",
      "name": "DNS as C2 in Noir, An AI-Developed Crypto Wallet Drainer",
      "description": "A cryptocurrency wallet-drainer kit called Noir uses DNS TXT records and DNS-over-HTTPS (DoH) as a dynamic command-and-control mechanism. The loader queries public DoH services to discover active infrastructure hosted on Cloudflare Pages, allowing operators to redirect deployed lures by changing a single DNS record. The drainer does not require victims to enter seed phrases or private keys; instead, it requests wallet connection permissions and obtains spending approvals that appear less suspicious than direct transfers. The architecture separates long-lived phishing lures from short-lived operational infrastructure, with 60-second DNS caching and self-healing retry logic. Extensive plain-English code comments suggest AI-assisted development, documenting bugs, fixes, and design decisions. The kit serves as a shared service across multiple cryptocurrency-themed phishing campaigns.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-12T23:10:55.357000",
      "created": "2026-10-09T22:03:27.940000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
