    {
      "id": "6ac9101554900e3ae83df111",
      "name": "The Scalpel vs. The Sledgehammer: Lessons in Precision Triage from the .conf26 SOC",
      "description": "During a live Security Operations Center shift at .conf26 in Denver, analysts investigated Incident ES_00244 involving an exploit link detected by Cisco Secure Firewall. The challenge arose when 15 devices were found communicating with a single IP address (13.226.251.40) flagged for hosting malicious domains moonlighthathel[.]org and ukankingwithea[.]com. Investigation revealed the IP was an Amazon CloudFront CDN node simultaneously serving legitimate services including Samsung Health, Mindtickle learning platform, and Amazon Video. Using AI-assisted analysis, firewall logs, and packet forensics through Endace, analysts isolated one unmanaged Intel laptop generating malicious traffic among 14 benign connections. Instead of blocking the shared IP and disrupting legitimate services, analysts implemented precise DNS object blocks targeting only the malicious domains at the Cisco Firepower Threat Defense perimeter, successfully neutralizing the threat while maintaining normal operations for all other attendees.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-12T23:05:38.825000",
      "created": "2026-10-09T16:02:29.260000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "",
