    {
      "id": "6ac84a155bb626a3710179b9",
      "name": "US disrupts Chinese hacking tools as 7 govts warn of PRC spies stealing sensitive data worldwide",
      "description": "The FBI seized seven web domains linked to Integrity Technology Group, a Chinese security firm allegedly providing hacking tools to Beijing-backed operatives. These tools enabled attacks on critical infrastructure, including a South Carolina power company and universities in Taiwan. The Flax Typhoon group utilized a Mirai-based botnet from 2021 to infect internet-connected devices, scan networks, and launch cyberattacks while concealing Chinese government hackers' locations. The malicious activity involved vulnerability scanning via Microscan tool, cross-site scripting, password spraying on Microsoft Exchange servers, and data exfiltration using FishHub malware. A joint advisory from US, UK, Australia, Canada, Japan, New Zealand, and Spain warned that Chinese state-sponsored actors continue targeting organizations worldwide to steal sensitive information from critical infrastructure networks.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-10-09T08:39:51.160000",
      "created": "2026-10-09T01:57:41.773000",
      "revision": 2,
