    {
      "id": "6ab4023773b652cd342e0854",
      "name": "VeloCloud Orchestrator Remote Access Vulnerability",
      "description": "VeloCloud Orchestrator (VCO) on-premises deployments contain a critical vulnerability allowing remote attackers to access privileged internal functionality and compromise the VCO host. The flaw, tracked as CVE-2026-93952 with a CVSS score of 10.0, enables attackers with network access to the VCO web interface and access to the public portion of VeloCloud Edge authentication certificates to exploit the system. This vulnerability is actively being exploited in the wild and affects VCO versions 5.2.3.15 and below, 6.1.3.7 and below, 6.4.2.7 and below, and 7.0.0.2 and below. Successful exploitation compromises confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the orchestrator and managed data. Hosted VCO versions were already patched. Specific indicators of compromise include malicious files, suspicious HTTP headers, and connections from known malicious IP addresses.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-09-23T19:45:56.614000",
      "created": "2026-09-23T16:45:43.415000",
