    {
      "id": "6ab22dd5026bef69ef5a17fd",
      "name": "AI Security Incident Case: Trusted AI Platforms Become a New Channel for Malware Distribution",
      "description": "This document analyzes multiple cybersecurity incidents involving various threat actors and malicious campaigns. The analysis covers sophisticated attack methodologies including exploitation of vulnerabilities, deployment of specialized malware tools, and targeting of critical infrastructure across multiple sectors. The campaigns demonstrate advanced persistent threat capabilities with focus on data exfiltration, system compromise, and lateral movement within targeted networks. Key observations include the use of social engineering tactics, exploitation of remote access vulnerabilities, and deployment of custom malware frameworks. The threat landscape encompasses government, technology, financial, and defense sectors with significant emphasis on supply chain attacks and credential harvesting operations.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-09-22T08:00:06.165000",
      "created": "2026-09-22T07:27:17.450000",
