    {
      "id": "6a7da6ccbbdd8552713c76a1",
      "name": "New Armored Likho tools target Telegram and eavesdropping",
      "description": "In May 2026, a new cyber-espionage campaign by the Armored Likho group targeted private individuals and organizations across Russia, including major corporations, public sector entities, IT companies, and educational institutions. The operation used fake donation service applications as initial infection vectors. The attackers deployed a new toolkit called Still Toolkit, written in Rust, comprising two components: Still Sync steals Telegram session data enabling automated extraction of chat logs, media files and account information through Telegram API; Still Audio performs covert audio surveillance by analyzing incoming audio streams, automatically detecting speech patterns, recording conversations and transmitting them to command-and-control servers. The campaign demonstrates significant evolution in the group's capabilities, utilizing shared infrastructure patterns and encryption techniques consistent with previous operations.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-09-12T11:19:01.787000",
      "created": "2026-08-13T11:13:16.563000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "Armored Likho",
