    {
      "id": "6a71a6ac7bd8297ea6d2093f",
      "name": "ClickFix-Themed Campaign Deploys Starland RAT and WLDR Framework",
      "description": "A Russian-speaking, financially motivated threat actor designated UAT-11795 has been conducting a sophisticated malware campaign since June 2025, primarily targeting users in the United States. The operation utilizes ClickFix-style social engineering techniques with trojanized software installers for applications like MobaXterm, Cisco WebEx, Zoom, DBeaver, and FACEIT. The campaign deploys Starland RAT, a custom Python-based remote access tool that establishes persistence, performs reconnaissance, and collects cryptocurrency wallet information. The malware employs blockchain-based fallback C2 mechanisms via Polygon smart contracts. Additionally, the operation deploys the previously undocumented WLDR PowerShell framework, CastleStealer, and Remcos RAT, demonstrating a modular architecture focused on credential theft, cryptocurrency harvesting, and long-term post-compromise access.",
      "author_name": "AlienVault",
      "modified": "2026-08-04T15:05:47.949000",
      "created": "2026-08-04T08:45:32.535000",
      "revision": 2,
      "tlp": "white",
      "public": 1,
      "adversary": "UAT-11795",
